{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted","id":103039,"title":"What is the inner struggle (Curse) for the Lunar Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-31T18:05:13-07:00","id":103039,"title":"What is the inner struggle (Curse) for the Lunar Exalted?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar thematics will be more tightly focused on the dualism of a &quot;good&quot; person who has a monster inside, or a monster who has a good person inside. Rage, transformation, and shapeshifting will be much more strongly evinced in their narrative and their mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cromage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of &quot;dualism&quot; but I'm not so keen on the &quot;human vs monster&quot; and have actually seen that more in the province of (gasp!) other splats (don't kill me). I like the idea of Lunars being champions of two worlds--exiles, outsiders, emigrants, and wanderers--and having to either choose one world or another or somehow trying to reconcile them.<br /> <br /> ETA: More importantly I always hated chimerism and its tendency to drag Lunars into really dumb places. Maybe 3e will make it not suck.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human vs. monster isn't on the schedule. I'm not turning Lunars into a werewolf story.<br /> <br /> Chimeraism is going to be way different in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miss Maddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent is the 'frenzy' aspect of the Lunar Exalted going to tied to all of this? Will Lunars be more emotional or moody? Will the Full Moon give limit? Will Lunar Limit breaks involve largely animal-themed expressions of primal emotion?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frenzy aspects are choice driven, not the default state of all Lunars. Full Moon insanity is getting tossed entirely out. Lunar Limit Breaks are undetermined, but are likely to change from what they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the above exchanges, I'm assuming that the Great Curse of the Lunar Exalted is not going to grant them a &quot;Man versus the Animal Within / Inner Monster&quot; narrative that reflects the Alchemical Host's &quot;man versus machine&quot; narrative (Clarity).<br /> <br /> Not having a Great Curse that drives the Lunars to fits of animal behavior also helps distinguish them from the Solar Exalted, who <i>do </i>have an &quot;inner monster&quot; struggle because their Great Curse drives them to fits of great passion (or fits of terrible dispassion).<br /> <br /> Still, what does that leave? Identity disassociation? Ie: Multiple personality disorder?<br /> <br /> <br /> Note that the inner struggle highlighted by their Great Curse may very well be completely distinct from their other inner struggle, which seems to center around their old but strong association with the Solar Exalted and how the disappearance of the Solars left the Lunar Exalted without a place in the world. The Lunar struggle to find a new purpose may be their reflection of Sidereal Arcane Fate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, to clarify the very first quotation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not big on the concept of dualism like this [between human and monster] in general, it seems to imply that there is some sort of necessary conflict between being a &quot;monster&quot; and a &quot;good person&quot; that require the two to be somehow separate.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely true, and largely phrased that way because if we had simply said &quot;Luna Exalts people who are monsters on the inside or the outside&quot; a lot of people would assume that we meant Lunars are Dexter, which, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-31-2014, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T19:54:58-07:00","id":103087,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's an exaggeration to say that the Lunar Exaltation transforms its host to a greater extent than any other. Everything about a Lunar changes, except maybe the soul. And it doesn't stop changing. Other Exalts get supernatural powers, but what Lunars get is a transformation into something truly beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend. It's not hard to imagine ways of building curse effects into that, even before the Primordials get involved.<br /> <br /> On another note, I'm glad to see the shift in language away from &quot;animal&quot;. Lunars have never really felt like the animal Exalted to me. Even in Second Edition, animals are just the first and easiest category of shapes, to be followed in time by raksha, ghost, elemental demon, etc. I much prefer <i>shapeless avatar of destruction</i> to <i>animal</i> any day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:12:54-07:00","id":103096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's an exaggeration to say that the Lunar Exaltation transforms its host to a greater extent than any other. Everything about a Lunar changes, except maybe the soul. And it doesn't stop changing. Other Exalts get supernatural powers, but what Lunars get is a transformation into something truly beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Infernals would like to say Hi while wearing your face and being totally dedicated to destroying all you love before removing themselves of all attachment and then hating you because they just saw you and you didn't repay their love by kneeling in abject submission and allowing them to carve out your free will. (In between holding a conversation with their physically embodied intimacies and turning into natural hazards the size of cities.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not hard to imagine ways of building curse effects into that, even before the Primordials get involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I'm glad to see the shift in language away from &quot;animal&quot;. Lunars have never really felt like the animal Exalted to me. Even in Second Edition, animals are just the first and easiest category of shapes, to be followed in time by raksha, ghost, elemental demon, etc. I much prefer <i>shapeless avatar of destruction</i> to <i>animal</i> any day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful, the way of Chimerism lies in the shapeless bit. Animals are a cheep way out, must like cutting off a finger as your sacrifice to sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:15:57-07:00","id":103098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's an exaggeration to say that the Lunar Exaltation transforms its host to a greater extent than any other. Everything about a Lunar changes, except maybe the soul. And it doesn't stop changing. Other Exalts get supernatural powers, but what Lunars get is a transformation into something truly beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a lot more like the Infernal Exalted of Second Edition. And they <i>did </i>go so far as to change the soul; at least in adding more of them right from the start, with the possibility of making many more. Even building an entire world within the soul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note, I'm glad to see the shift in language away from &quot;animal&quot;. Lunars have never really felt like the animal Exalted to me. Even in Second Edition, animals are just the first and easiest category of shapes, to be followed in time by raksha, ghost, elemental demon, etc </div> </div> </div>Well, I can provide an exact quote from John to the extent that the Lunars won't be the Animal Exalted, in the sense of &quot;National Geographic&quot; (my words, not his).<br /> <br /> There may be pistol shrimp and bombardier beetles and electric eels in the wild, and Lunars can get those abilities by assuming those forms, but John tells us that Lunar Charms aren't going to revolve around giving Lunars those &quot;National Geographic&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> The Nemean Lion to which John points us had impenetrable skin and armor-cutting claws. Easily the result of Stamina and Strength Charms applied to a normal lion shape.<br /> <br /> Rather than Animal Exalted, the Lunars seem to be going for Animal-God Exalted. Like, if Zeus was more heavily themed around the shape of his favored bird, the eagle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I much prefer <i>shapeless avatar of destruction</i> to <i>animal</i> any day. </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is that one shapeless avatar of destruction would look and play exactly like any other shapeless avatar of destruction.<br /> <br /> I imagine the the developers are deliberately steering away from &quot;formlessness is the optimal condition&quot;. That's boring even for Fair Folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:20:00-07:00","id":103102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Exalts get supernatural powers, but what Lunars get is a transformation into something truly beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Lunars is beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend?<br /> <br /> They are a PC splat. It they were incomprehensible, I think they'd be a bit harder to play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I'm glad to see the shift in language away from &quot;animal&quot;. Lunars have never really felt like the animal Exalted to me. Even in Second Edition, animals are just the first and easiest category of shapes, to be followed in time by raksha, ghost, elemental demon, etc. I much prefer <i>shapeless avatar of destruction</i> to <i>animal</i> any day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think animals are good. They're simple to hook into and come with a nice range of symbolism while fitting the shaman/barbarian warrior/trickster idea better than elementals of shapeless avatars of anything.<br /> <br /> I don't see destruction as a Lunar thing. They can wreck your face, but that's because of their raw, primal power. There's nothing inherently destructive about said power though. It could also be used to create or transform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-31-2014, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:57:56-07:00","id":103122,"title":"","content":"If Jekyll and Hyde isn't on the table, perhaps Ratkin Rapture is. They were &quot;Gnosis frenzies&quot; that imparted distorted visions and premonitions when the rat was too much in tune with the spirit world. It included a number of effects that would be similar to being delusional, paranoid, etc., in addition to more mystical consequences like tuning out the world of matter and seeing only the spiritual landscape of the world.<br /> <br /> Going off of that last point, it might end up changing perceptions in a matter similar to the protagonist of Saya no Uta, who sees (and hears, and smells and otherwise perceives) humans as horrible, monstrous creatures and vice versa. The trailer for Oculus also comes to mind, but it's painful like that episode of Clone High where Abe's mouth keeps getting cut up, so beware.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103087#post103087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's an exaggeration to say that the Lunar Exaltation transforms its host to a greater extent than any other. Everything about a Lunar changes, except maybe the soul. And it doesn't stop changing. Other Exalts get supernatural powers, but what Lunars get is a transformation into something truly beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend. It's not hard to imagine ways of building curse effects into that, even before the Primordials get involved.<br /> <br /> On another note, I'm glad to see the shift in language away from &quot;animal&quot;. Lunars have never really felt like the animal Exalted to me. Even in Second Edition, animals are just the first and easiest category of shapes, to be followed in time by raksha, ghost, elemental demon, etc. I much prefer <i>shapeless avatar of destruction</i> to <i>animal</i> any day.</div> </div> </div> </div>About that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Lunar spoiler #1: Disclaimer: This is not a spoiler about their Charm set. Their Charms are distinct from what I am about to describe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Beasts (animals, dinosaurs, monsters) are different from what they were in previous editions. More than just statblocks acting as minor obstacles, many creatures a Lunar can shapeshift into use special abilities that a Lunar can borrow when taking that animal's form. Some beasts are actually very robust competent hunters and fighters, such as the Tyrant Lizard. A Lunar using that form can extend tracking (Survival) rolls across an entire continent using the Tyrant Lizard's incredible sense of smell. And in a fight, she can learn to use the Tyrant Lizard's signature attacks, including his finisher, Ferocious Bite, which is a pants-shittingly terrifying attack.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Each animal form has advantages and extends the Lunar a mechanical toolbox to play with.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke[COLOR=#000000</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">]</span>[/COLOR]<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">It is still the animal you choose to be the basis for your DBT. How much I force it into your character's appearance remains to be seen. If you don't want to be a DBT Lunar, I'd rather you think of DBT / spirit shape as the tool you relied on when your Lunar was still young, inexperienced, and less powerful, rather than ignoring it entirely. I want to help people build away from a DBT-based character through powers that work when you are in your human form and don't work when you are in DBT.<br /> <br /> Once you reach that point, it is my intention that the spirit shape, through a clever use of keywords and associations, provide you a favored discount on Charms whose Attributes you don't favor, going so far as to change the Charm's prerequisites and shift it to a logical place in your current Charm trees (if one exists). So even if you ignore your spirit shape in roleplay, its themes are there helping you by providing a framework to power up your character.<br /> <br /> I also realize that one of the reasons people search so furiously for meaning beyond DBT is because a single animal is so constraining, so I am looking at completely redoing Chimeraism so that it is an accepted state, so that players can make cool-looking hybrid monsters with lots of different traits.<br /> <br /> Note that everything I've said here is &quot;Maybe&quot; not &quot;I promise&quot; and is subject to change. This is about as far as I am willing to reach into my giant vault of future noise to show people, but I feel like the general tone of acceptance and readiness for big new ideas has reached a level where such a classified view won't confuse and upset anyone.</div></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">&quot;Werewolf-inspired Exalted&quot; is arguably an even richer concept-mine than &quot;Frankenstein-inspired Exalted.&quot; [1] Taking the oWoD's particular interpretation of werewolves as both a solid starting point and a limiter for exploring the concept is a terrible mistake, though.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">[1] Particularly when you expand &quot;Frankenstein&quot; to &quot;all tales of created life or unnatural outcasts are fair game for inspiration,&quot; and particularly when you expand &quot;werewolf&quot; to &quot;all tales of bestial dualism, and all shapeshifting folklore of any kind.&quot; I mean, hardly anyone in America has ever even heard of them, but I could riff on African werehyena legends alone pretty much forever. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TFsjoAHIscY\" target=\"_blank\">The Last Warrior fights on!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:01:16-07:00","id":103125,"title":"","content":"I think the inner struggle should be based, generally, on what their purpose is in the big narrative of the game. I really hope that is locked down a lot more solidly in 3E, as I think they were not needed as a narrative group in 2E (note: I never played 1E). I hope 3E isn't a wishy-washy &quot;they kinda do this and kinda do that - depending on the author/writer&quot;, as it was frustrating for a new GM to the game in 2E to figure out what to do with them in the big picture. They kinda remind me of Boba Fett; somebody who is super cool, but I don't think actually <i>did</i> anything. I'm really hoping their inner struggle is something a new player can grasp on to and run with that feels untamed and raw. Not in a &quot;me versus cultivated society&quot; kind of way, but more in a &quot;nature is powerful and bad-ass!&quot; kind of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/466-poop-deck","name":"Poop Deck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar466_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:36:40-07:00","id":103145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103098#post103098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nemean Lion to which John points us had impenetrable skin and armor-cutting claws. Easily the result of Stamina and Strength Charms applied to a normal lion shape.<br /> <br /> Rather than Animal Exalted, the Lunars seem to be going for Animal-God Exalted. Like, if Zeus was more heavily themed around the shape of his favored bird, the eagle.</div> </div> </div> </div>This and the notes on DBT sound like a perfectly good start; Lunars start out taking forms like legendary creatures, and can either double down there or move into other areas of shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> While I am likely to homebrew in pistol shrimp and moonwitch and quantum-physics-reference charms, legendary beast shapeshifting is nice solid ground to build on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:39:40-07:00","id":103149,"title":"","content":"OK, I'll bite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103102#post103102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see destruction as a Lunar thing. They can wreck your face, but that's because of their raw, primal power. There's nothing inherently destructive about said power though. It could also be used to create or transform.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually been making that same point on other threads just in the past few days. When I said I preferred being a shapeless avatar of destruction to being an animal, I wasn't putting forward destruction as some kind of core Lunar theme. I was just giving an example of something more interesting to me than <i>animal.</i> If I'd been feeling more creative, I would have probably thrown out a few other examples, but I didn't think I needed to.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I tend to play No Moons with problem-solving abilities and intelligence and perception/insight charms. But all of those characters still have war forms, and yeah, in those forms, they tend toward shapelessness (by which I mean near-chimerism via HBR), weirdness, and either destructive potential or invulnerability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103102#post103102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Lunars is beyond the ability of human minds to comprehend?<br /> <br /> They are a PC splat. It they were incomprehensible, I think they'd be a bit harder to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I'm probably going to provoke some argument. As you say, Lunars embody raw power. I totally agree, but I think it works slightly better to say they embody potential, since it's really their capacity for change that gives them their power. And that capacity is infinite. If you're a Lunar, you've been transformed into something quite incomprehensible to a mortal mind: something without limits. And that is probably a very scary thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:43:33-07:00","id":103153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103096#post103096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Infernals would like to say Hi while wearing your face and being totally dedicated to destroying all you love before removing themselves of all attachment and then hating you because they just saw you and you didn't repay their love by kneeling in abject submission and allowing them to carve out your free will. (In between holding a conversation with their physically embodied intimacies and turning into natural hazards the size of cities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Infernals change. I'm not certain anything can actually do &quot;change&quot; more than Lunars, but I probably would have given Infernals a mention as possible contenders if I'd thought of them. It was just that I was really only thinking of the &quot;original&quot; Exaltations, not the more recent Solar derivatives. Although with 3E, maybe Infernals aren't Solaroids anymore? I'm not sure how that works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103096#post103096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Careful, the way of Chimerism lies in the shapeless bit. Animals are a cheep way out, must like cutting off a finger as your sacrifice to sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with chimerism itself. It's just unfortunate that it's always accompanied by madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T22:39:24-07:00","id":103185,"title":"","content":"I have to say, Lunar fans are strange. Especially Lunar fans new to the forums. They seem to have this poetic streak about them when they talk about what Lunars are to them, what their symbolism is, and so on, it's rather bizarre.<br /> <br /> Case in point, does anybody else remember Chris-A-Rose? Because I swear I've seen... Well not the same arguments, but the same tone of arguments before, a very similar style. How odd.<br /> <br /> At any rate, TSk, I really fear that Infernals pretty much hijacked what you wanted Lunars to be like. You'd probably want them to be much more... Complicated, than where they seem to go in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T22:50:25-07:00","id":103193,"title":"","content":"How is that bizarre?<br /> <br /> How do older fans talk about Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:27:43-07:00","id":103217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103185#post103185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At any rate, TSk, I really fear that Infernals pretty much hijacked what you wanted Lunars to be like. You'd probably want them to be much more... Complicated, than where they seem to go in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think I'm just terrible at getting my point across... because this is really the opposite of what I think. No, I don't want Lunars to be more complicated. It's one of the more appealing things about them that they're uncomplicated. They're raw and primal. Not like Infernals or even Solars.<br /> <br /> Devil-tigers are nice, yes. Infernals can obviously transform. But it's a different kind of transformation, and they can only do it at high essence, and can really only transform into one kind of thing that way, a Primordial. They can't change into ghosts or raksha or even into animals, really. And forget about mixing around all three. And when you think about it... is a Primordial really more different from a human than a human is from a manta ray? I'm not sure. See the ongoing discussion about the dickishness of Primordials for that one.<br /> <br /> There are things I'd do differently, but no, I don't actually think any Exalt was hijacked and I don't think any is broken and unplayable. I seem to be in the minority of players, in that I actually really like the game and pretty much everything in it.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not that other person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T00:40:33-07:00","id":103251,"title":"","content":"'Infernals did it' is a very bad reason to deny any of the core splats of Exalted anything, really.<br /> <br /> Lunars should be what Lunars should be, not what conflicts with Infernals or not; at the end of the day, most things do, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T00:57:48-07:00","id":103258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103217#post103217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think I'm just terrible at getting my point across... because this is really the opposite of what I think. No, I don't want Lunars to be more complicated. It's one of the more appealing things about them that they're uncomplicated. They're raw and primal. Not like Infernals or even Solars.<br /> <br /> Devil-tigers are nice, yes. Infernals can obviously transform. But it's a different kind of transformation, and they can only do it at high essence, and can really only transform into one kind of thing that way, a Primordial. They can't change into ghosts or raksha or even into animals, really. And forget about mixing around all three. And when you think about it... is a Primordial really more different from a human than a human is from a manta ray? I'm not sure. See the ongoing discussion about the dickishness of Primordials for that one.<br /> <br /> There are things I'd do differently, but no, I don't actually think any Exalt was hijacked and I don't think any is broken and unplayable. I seem to be in the minority of players, in that I actually really like the game and pretty much everything in it.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not that other person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're not, wasn't suggesting that. You're certainly your own man TSk. Or a woman. Or something else entirely. But unique individual, yes.<br /> <br /> All I really can say about your interpretation of Lunars is that it's certainly a valid one. A strong one and interesting one to boot. One which I could embrace, would gladly utilize and will potentially steal from you at some point!<br /> <br /> However... To be honest I'm not sure how well the mechanics of Lunar will correspond with your vision. Because the way I see it, Lunars aren't so much about not-very-well-defined &quot;potential&quot; and change as &quot;infinite possibilities&quot;, but more about straight-forward adaptation of various monster myths and folk legends in Exalted. I certainly don't think of shapeshifting as their defining feature, more like a tool in their arsenal, they are shapeshifters, but not by definition. So if mechanics reflect this, you might have trouble adapting.<br /> <br /> But I certainly wish you good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-01-2014, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T01:43:17-07:00","id":103264,"title":"","content":"Since i've ever played or read oWoD Werewolf anyone care to explain what this Rage is and what they may be drawing from it? I feel that may have something to do with their inner struggle but I need more context. I also find it incredibly interesting that the distinction between transformation and shape shifting is made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T01:56:21-07:00","id":103266,"title":"","content":"IIRC, as Luna's chosen warriors they were filled with divine Rage. It empowered them (you could spend rage points to get extra actions, for example) but also the higher your rage, the more likely you were to flip out and attack people in a mad frenzy, possibly including your pack-mates. While in Frenzy you ignored wound penalties though.<br /> The more fighty auspices (classes, essentially) had more rage than the trickster and shaman auspices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T03:35:02-07:00","id":103290,"title":"","content":"I'm on a kick of thinking about the big 5 Exalt types in terms defined by their Alchemical Caste analogues at the moment, because it just feels really useful, and I feel like Neph did a pretty great job of distilling the essence of each of the 5 splats when he wrote them.<br /> <br /> See - <a href=\"http://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2010/05/18/exalted-alchemicals-orichalcum-caste/\" target=\"_blank\">http://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.co...chalcum-caste/</a> for Octopoid breaking this down.<br /> <br /> So thinking about the Solars and why their Curse is appropriate from this perspective -<br /> <br /> Orichalcum Caste Alchemicals express the idea of raw power rather than finesse or endurance.<br /> <br /> Like them, the Solars are all about having the most power and skill, not about enduring when they lose (e.g. their patron has the sobriquet &quot;unconquered&quot;, not who has been conquered yet overcome) or using the power and skill they have in an agile or clever manner.<br /> <br /> (The Solars do certainly have Charms that express clever use of resources or endurance, but they express the Solar theme of overcoming through overwhelming power and skill through abilities that are about cleverly using resources or enduring.<br /> <br /> The Solars don't have clever, dextrous efficient use of power woven through their splat's design like it is a theme for Sidereals [who are efficient, pragmatic and work cleverly under restrictions], and although they have survival Charms, survivorship and enduring and being stronger because they can endure isn't woven across into their splat's themes and Charms).<br /> <br /> Compare John Morke's take on the Solars, contrasted with the other Celestials - <i>Solars are myth-heroes. It is a myth-hero's purpose to subvert mythos and thereby define it. Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large</i>.<br /> <br /> So the Solar Curse is &quot;being confronted with my limits of my power and capabilities drives me mad&quot; - I mean, it's even called limit break (i.e. they break up, psychologically, when they realise they reach their limit).<br /> <br /> So what are Lunars about in a comparable way?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2010/05/18/exalted-alchemicals-moonsilver-caste/\" target=\"_blank\">http://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.co...nsilver-caste/</a> &quot;<i>the Lunars are adaptive and fluid, so too are the Moonsilver Alchemicals... Through adaptability, speed of body and thought, and the ability to blend with any surrounding do the Moonsilver Caste serve their nations</i>.&quot;.<br /> <br /> and Lunars are about survivorship and enduring and being able to come back stronger because they endure.<br /> <br /> (Lunar surivorship feels like it has too often been handled as &quot;they just survive&quot;, like Cockroachman, not &quot;because they are enduring they can come back stronger and ultimately achieve more than the more obviously powerful and efficient, but brittle, splats&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's why they're the survivors of a war of attrition, that's why they make sense to have an internal struggle, partly why they make sense as monsters as a characteristic of monsters tend to be ridiculous degrees of resilience. It's even why 1e and 2e (perhaps not entirely correctly) made them the splat that focused on building an enduring way of mortal living that could survive, in contrast to the brittleness of the powerful, but vulnerable, High Modernist First Age.<br /> <br /> So their Curse should relate to straining the limits of that power, the power to quickly adapt and change and survive and overcome by doing so.<br /> <br /> But here's where I come unstuck. What's an actual good curse that fits with this? Chimerism (as it's a form of the ability to adapt and survive turned malignant)...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T04:41:02-07:00","id":103301,"title":"","content":"Lunars, Sidereal and Infernals all change themselves. <br /> <br /> A Lunar changes his body and his mind, but he keeps his soul and his Essence stable. The Lunar's soul forms a solid core of identity which the Lunar can always use, both to draw strength from, and to always remember what he or she is. When a Lunar's soul (core) gets changed too much, they loose track of what they are and begin turning into a Chimera. That's what the idea behind Permanent Limit represents. <br /> <br /> Sidereal's change their Essence. Martial Arts allows a Sidereal to change his Essence pattern, which lets him mimic other beings or concepts. The Sidereal doesn't actually transform into a spider, but when using Charcoal March of the Spiders, the Sidereal's Essence alters itself to reflect the Essence of Spiders, and that, along with specific spider-like movements, gives the Sidereal power from the concept of spiders. With a few exceptions, Sidereals keep their own minds, bodies and souls fairly stable. <br /> <br /> Infernals change everything about themselves. Their bodies, their minds, their souls and their Essence patterns. As they do so, they begin to grow more and more inhuman and monstrous. While a Lunar is better at altering his body or mind, and a Sidereal is better at altering his Essence, nobody is able to sculpt themselves in so many different ways as an Infernal can.<br /> <br /> Other splats (Alchemicals and Abyssals especially) also change and alter themselves in different ways. The Alchemical's growth into a massive city is closer to the direction of Infernals, as their minds, bodies and souls becoming something else. Abyssals meanwhile have charms which allow them to begin carving off their living natures and embracing the emptiness of the Underworld. But theirs is more of a mutilation than an alteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T05:18:24-07:00","id":103314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SurlySeraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103145#post103145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I am likely to homebrew in pistol shrimp and moonwitch and quantum-physics-reference charms, legendary beast shapeshifting is nice solid ground to build on.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't say they wouldn't have Charms to enhance the effects of a pistol shrimp's attack, mind you. Just that they probably wouldn't have Charms to emulate fire sparking in any form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T05:35:53-07:00","id":103320,"title":"","content":"I really don't want any &quot;Beaver build dam good =&gt; Lunar build dam good too!&quot; charms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T06:50:34-07:00","id":103353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103290#post103290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Solars don't have clever, dextrous efficient use of power woven through their splat's design</div> </div> </div> </div>Night Caste.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:14:46-07:00","id":103363,"title":"","content":"Seems like a misguided and dismissive way to miss the point and decontextualize a quote, or I'm very, very poor at expressing myself.<br /> <br /> (Although if you really do think that spouting &quot;Night Caste&quot; is good evidence that the Solars have using limited power efficiently and cleverly (not wisely) weaved throughout their whole splat's themes in the way it is to say Sidereals...which I guess you must otherwise you wouldn't have said it.... then that's probably a good point for us to leave this discussion on.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:18:24-07:00","id":103366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103320#post103320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't want any &quot;Beaver build dam good =&gt; Lunar build dam good too!&quot; charms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then with less fear may you face the world to come:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't plan on turning Lunars into the Animal Exalted, because there are a few problems with that premise:<br /> <br /> 1) Animal powers using animal logic go in a Sci-Fi direction, unfitting for a mythology world.<br /> <br /> 2) Animal powers being the source of your awesome power makes you feel like the Chosen of Zoo Tycoon.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we get rid of the spirit shape or animal associations for some of their magic. That does mean that we probably don't want their Charm set being modeled in its entirety after Things Animals Do\u2122. A mythic association is cool here and there (Graceful Crane Stance, Ten Ox Meditation), but when my greatest intelligence Charm is based on an elephant or a dolphin I start to feel like a monkey, and the whole Charm set starts to look like Jump the Shark Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:19:22-07:00","id":103367,"title":"","content":"This is one of those topics where I feel like it will be vastly easier to speculate once the corebook is out. There are two big lacunae in the way of guesses: we don't know what Lunars look like in Third Edition, and we don't know what the Solar Curse looks like in Third Edition. The dev comments on these two subjects have been interesting, but they're pretty thin grounds for extrapolation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:20:09-07:00","id":103369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103353#post103353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Night Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah, the subtle, clever, efficient Night Caste<br /> <br /> Night Caste Athletics: Jump over mountains<br /> Night Caste Awareness: My burning eyes banish all lies and illusions<br /> Night Caste Dodge: I turn into sunlight to avoid the volcano<br /> Night Caste Larceny: The door won't open. I walk through the door.<br /> Night Caste Stealth: IGNORE MEEEEEE","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1538-jonsonjonson","name":"JonsonJonson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:50:46-07:00","id":103390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103369#post103369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yeah, the subtle, clever, efficient Night Caste<br /> <br /> Night Caste Athletics: Jump over mountains<br /> Night Caste Awareness: My burning eyes banish all lies and illusions<br /> Night Caste Dodge: I turn into sunlight to avoid the volcano<br /> Night Caste Larceny: The door won't open. I walk through the door.<br /> Night Caste Stealth: IGNORE MEEEEEE</div> </div> </div> </div>You will notice that aside from Stealth, all the effects you list are high-Essence right ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:39:50-07:00","id":103411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103264#post103264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since i've ever played or read oWoD Werewolf anyone care to explain what this Rage is and what they may be drawing from it? I feel that may have something to do with their inner struggle but I need more context. I also find it incredibly interesting that the distinction between transformation and shape shifting is made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna loves Gaia. Mankind has taken Gaia, chained her in down in its basement, and spent the last century beating and raping her. Werewolves are Luna's warriors and they draw power from her Rage. The problem is that Luna is at the 'just fucking kill them all' stage, so Werewolves have spiritual anger management issues that leads to them slaughtering their way through all manner of problems and situations.<br /> <br /> But it doesn't matter because Gaia is beyond hope, and you, for all your terrifying strength and power, are not saving the world but raging impotently over its broken corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 04-01-2014, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:51:15-07:00","id":103417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103264#post103264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since i've ever played or read oWoD Werewolf anyone care to explain what this Rage is and what they may be drawing from it? I feel that may have something to do with their inner struggle but I need more context. I also find it incredibly interesting that the distinction between transformation and shape shifting is made.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In Werewolf, you have this stat called Rage. For every dot that you have in Rage, you are ten times angrier than Henry Rollins - all the time.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was a 1-10 stat like Willpower. If it was over your Willpower, you got penalties to social rolls. If it was over the Willpower of non-monsters around you, you also got social penalties when dealing with them. Aside from being usable to move and attack faster than normal, it also allowed for quick shapeshifting, shaking off being stunned (much more serious in the classic WoD, because it forfeited your entire turn after getting hit), some limited mollification of wound penalties, and there were some powers to expand its use. However, if you lost all of it and your Willpower, you lost the wolf, and couldn't change from breed form or regain Rage (normally accomplished by being on the bad side of a situation or looking at the moon) until you psychologically salvaged yourself.<br /> <br /> In character, even having one dot in it meant that you were angrier than humanly possible. It made everyone else uneasy, as reflected through the penalties to interact with others. There was also the possibility of going berserk when you rolled the stat, since a number of successes would make you frenzy. Too many could push you into Thrall of the Wyrm, wherein some werewolves would do terrible things under the influence of their fury, like attack allies... and then eat them.<br /> <br /> Addendum: forgot about Rage recovery. You could revive yourself, possibly, at the cost of automatically flipping out. It wasn't quite like the Charms that stop damage at your last -4, though. Halfway between that and Luna's Fortitude. You'd end up getting horrible, lasting injuries that didn't quite heal correctly, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-01-2014, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:52:21-07:00","id":103419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103411#post103411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luna loves Gaia. Mankind has taken Gaia, chained her in down in its basement, and spent the last century beating and raping her. Werewolves are Luna's warriors and they draw power from her Rage. The problem is that Luna is at the 'just fucking kill them all' stage, so Werewolves have spiritual anger management issues that leads to them slaughtering their way through all manner of problems and situations.<br /> <br /> <b>But it doesn't matter because Gaia is beyond hope</b>, and you, for all your terrifying strength and power, are not saving the world but raging impotently over its broken corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as of the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix in W20.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:58:24-07:00","id":103424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103258#post103258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However... To be honest I'm not sure how well the mechanics of Lunar will correspond with your vision. Because the way I see it, Lunars aren't so much about not-very-well-defined &quot;potential&quot; and change as &quot;infinite possibilities&quot;, but more about straight-forward adaptation of various monster myths and folk legends in Exalted. I certainly don't think of shapeshifting as their defining feature, more like a tool in their arsenal, they are shapeshifters, but not by definition. So if mechanics reflect this, you might have trouble adapting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to think of shapeshifting as more defining of Lunars than animal, yeah. I mean, in 2nd Edition, a Lunar at Essence 6 can eat third-circle demons and absorb their powers (Essential Mirror Form was later errata'd for obvious reasons). Luna is the god/dess of moon, not of animal. But animal can still be part of it. Where they're going sounds interesting enough so far. And thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103290#post103290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Solar Curse is &quot;being confronted with my limits of my power and capabilities drives me mad&quot; - I mean, it's even called limit break (i.e. they break up, psychologically, when they realise they reach their limit).<br /> <br /> So what are Lunars about in a comparable way?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2010/05/18/exalted-alchemicals-moonsilver-caste/\" target=\"_blank\">http://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.co...nsilver-caste/</a> &quot;<i>the Lunars are adaptive and fluid, so too are the Moonsilver Alchemicals... Through adaptability, speed of body and thought, and the ability to blend with any surrounding do the Moonsilver Caste serve their nations</i>.&quot;.<br /> <br /> and Lunars are about survivorship and enduring and being able to come back stronger because they endure.<br /> <br /> (Lunar surivorship feels like it has too often been handled as &quot;they just survive&quot;, like Cockroachman, not &quot;because they are enduring they can come back stronger and ultimately achieve more than the more obviously powerful and efficient, but brittle, splats&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's why they're the survivors of a war of attrition, that's why they make sense to have an internal struggle, partly why they make sense as monsters as a characteristic of monsters tend to be ridiculous degrees of resilience. It's even why 1e and 2e (perhaps not entirely correctly) made them the splat that focused on building an enduring way of mortal living that could survive, in contrast to the brittleness of the powerful, but vulnerable, High Modernist First Age.<br /> <br /> So their Curse should relate to straining the limits of that power, the power to quickly adapt and change and survive and overcome by doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Second Edition, there was an attempt to say that Lunar Charms (and Knacks) are different in that they're not learned techniques and don't come from training. In other words, you're not actually learning better ways of shapeshifting as you get older; you already kind of know them as soon as you Exalt. But not really. It was never fully explained, so I just treated it as the case that humans were never meant to be technically limitless in form, and so the human mind tends to impose limits onto something that would otherwise be without them. So Lunar enlightenment with higher essence mostly just involves forgetting those restrictions, as your mortal identity becomes less important to you.<br /> <br /> So where I was going with my earlier comment was that an innate kind of Lunar curse sounds less to me like &quot;straining the limits of your power&quot; than maybe going too deep into your power and losing yourself in it. Permanent Limit sounds like a potentially useful idea for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:05:00-07:00","id":103425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103424#post103424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to think of shapeshifting as more defining of Lunars than animal, yeah. I mean, in 2nd Edition, a Lunar at Essence 6 can eat third-circle demons and absorb their powers (Essential Mirror Form was later errata'd for obvious reasons). Luna is the god/dess of moon, not of animal. But animal can still be part of it. Where they're going sounds interesting so far. And thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's quite well vested in beasts, given her Athletics specialty, and that her power causes her Chosen to develop totemic spirit shapes that can only arise from the beasts of her lover Gaia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:16:35-07:00","id":103434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103419#post103419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not as of the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix in W20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the one where the world ends... but something not-so-shitty may or may not happen afterwards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:36:00-07:00","id":103450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103369#post103369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yeah, the subtle, clever, efficient Night Caste</div> </div> </div> </div>They damn well should be, otherwise their Caste write up tells outright lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Night Caste Stealth: IGNORE MEEEEEE</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know from whence came the meme that this exemplified Solar Stealth more than being really hard to say, but I want to find the personification of that place and then eat its puppies.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, there's a point worth making that there are no &quot;Night Caste Charms&quot;; there are Solar Charms, almost equally accessible by all Castes, but with different assumptions in how they'd be applied, so that a Night Caste would be the sort to apply them with a measure of care and intricacy because that's what a Night Caste <i>is</i>. That being said, Awareness, Dodge, Stealth and Larceny are somewhat... passive Abilities. You've got two that are less about exerting effects against the world than evading stuff somebody else is doing, one which doesn't exert effects at all, instead improving the range of sensory data you can access, and another that is ultimately very context defined (being able to steal or disguise as anything might assume a bit of discernment in what you're actually taking or pretending to be).<br /> <br /> But hey, the Dodge cascade is huge now, there are reports of characters built entirely around Awareness, and Holden and Lioness apparently adore Larceny now, so maybe those Abilities will actually have a bit of granularity that makes the ethos of the Night Caste come across as having a bit more credibility, eh?<br /> <br /> I'd also hang some hopes off of the idea that Athletics doesn't quite have the same &quot;cross incredible distances with minimal effort&quot; bit again. Since that was literally the first thing I asked about Third Edition, and the answer I got was &quot;yes&quot;. Maybe less &quot;leap straight over the mountain&quot; and more &quot;move around local terrain with more intricacy that lets you define the angles of your action&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-01-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:43:25-07:00","id":103458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103450#post103450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know from whence came the meme that this exemplified Solar Stealth more than being really hard to say, but I want to find the personification of that place and then eat its puppies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charm is called Mental Invisibility Technique. It's under Stealth charms in the core rulebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103425#post103425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's quite well vested in beasts, given her Athletics specialty, and that her power causes her Chosen to develop totemic spirit shapes that can only arise from the beasts of her lover Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. I just meant I think she's more invested in the idea of <i>moon.</i> Although that might actually be wrong, come to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-01-2014, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:47:03-07:00","id":103461,"title":"","content":"I feel like the difference between Lunar and Infernal shapeshifting is being a bit overcomplicated around here.<br /> <br /> All I know is that, when I think of something that shapeshifts in the same basic paradigm of therianthrope legends, and something that would shapeshift into, say, Angels from Evangelion, the idea of them both being the same thing feels kind of silly.<br /> <br /> Not least because, if one portends the idea of them both together, the animal based one seems a lot less attractive. It's like how when people run away with high-concept supernatural martial arts too much, animal emulation styles seem to have a lot less focus and overall seem less interesting, even though that stuff has stronger credibility in the root source of supernatural martial arts in the first place.<br /> <br /> And then there's the whole problem that if Lunars, or anybody else, has <i>too</i> much variety to them, they don't really feel so much like different examples of the same thing, which would seem to kind of undermine the point of them existing as a group in the first place.<br /> <br /> I also have problems with stuff that might frame Infernals in terms that seem to kind of go in the opposite direction to this:<br /> &quot;It will include transhumanism, alien otherness, and monstrosity, but<br /> all of this will be carried by a core of mortal heroes raised up by<br /> their own power and philosophy, thus upholding the main tenet<br /> of Exalted\u2014that your character is central to the narrative, the<br /> hero, champion and singular force who can make her / his mark<br /> on the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> but that's really a more incidental point, and one I've discussed elsewhere anyway.<br /> <br /> Really, I'm <i>relieved</i> by the idea of Infernals being at least one place that certain forms of shapeshifting can be outsourced to so that Lunars can regain a measure of thematic purity. Same goes with quantum-mechanics Charms or whatever. I never really felt that Lunars were served well by becoming the dumping ground for every halfway interesting new idea that people had for Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:58:31-07:00","id":103471,"title":"","content":"It just seems that what Infernals (and Alchemicals) do is really more of an evolution than a simple embodiment of change. They can become Primordials or sci-fi megacities... but it's pretty much a one-way thing. They don't, reflexively, shift into a different Primordial or a different megacity on every tick. They don't mutate and combine the traits of cities and Primordials with a dozen other things. And most of them never even undergo that transformation in the first place. It's really only something a very few (in the case of Infernals, potentially none) ever achieve in-setting.<br /> <br /> I can appreciate how, in a sense, Infernals might embody potential/change more than anyone else, because there really are no <i>theoretical</i> limits to what they can eventually become. But that's technically true of any Exalt, really. And in another sense, their capacity for change is really a lot more restricted.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I just don't see transformation is what they're really about. If Triumphant Howl of the Devil-Tiger had never been written, would we even be connecting them with the idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-01-2014, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T10:11:39-07:00","id":103477,"title":"","content":"I feel like the inner struggle of the Lunar might not be a conflict, but rather a side of them that leaves them with a fairly powerful passion for the taboo or the extreme, something that can carry their reason along with it, and that many will allow it to*.<br /> <br /> Might be some conflict in the sense that Lunars need to anchor themselves down with some things so that passions and wild abandon don't carry them off completely. Solars and moonsilver tattoos might help with that some.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse is in there somewhere, but I'm not quite sure where; I'm attached to the idea that the raging inner storm that needs to be kept in check is the good and natural state of the Lunar, so their manifestation of the Curse is something else... Maybe at one time it was being too heavily devoted to and dependent on the Solars, and then informed their evolution through the Second Age along lines of &quot;let's become the monsters everybody is saying we are&quot;...<br /> <br /> Hmm, the natural state of Lunars being highly individual, to the point of needing certain restraints based on their context within relationships to others, with their Great Curse as a force to make them <i>too much</i> what other people might observe them as being, rather than being themselves... Could be fitting.<br /> <br /> * Of course, if there's a side of &quot;monster with 'good' person inside&quot;, there's also the chance for those sorts who are more given to the extreme and iconoclastic as a default, and the sort of oppositional impulses take the form of an inner voice of restraint. Which... actually kind of leaves me wondering at a possibility for a Lunar on the opposite extreme of mindless abandon; somebody so restrained and ascetic that they can barely manage to do anything at all. It's putting me in mind a bit of Werewolf: the Forsaken's new Harmony...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T10:20:31-07:00","id":103481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103450#post103450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They damn well should be, otherwise their Caste write up tells outright lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Exalted! Where different authors do different things with different ideas and for different reasons!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:08:36-07:00","id":103503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103477#post103477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the inner struggle of the Lunar might not be a conflict, but rather a side of them that leaves them with a fairly powerful passion for the taboo or the extreme, something that can carry their reason along with it, and that many will allow it to*.<br /> <br /> Might be some conflict in the sense that Lunars need to anchor themselves down with some things so that passions and wild abandon don't carry them off completely. Solars and moonsilver tattoos might help with that some.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be both plausible and thematic. I think I should clarify, though: when I said losing yourself in your power, I didn't mean going crazy with werewolf rage or just generally losing control. I meant losing your identity<br /> <br /> Lunars accomplish what they do, largely, by changing their shapes, including the shapes of their minds. All it takes to imagine a Lunar curse is to consider the effects of that. When you've transformed your own mind often enough, I expect you'll start to forget who you used to be, what you were like, what it was that made you believe the things you used to believe. Over their long millennia of continual change, I think it would be inevitable for Lunar Exalts to lose their human identities and simply stop being who and what they were. A mad Solar god-king may allow his virtue and perfection to consume him, but he's still a human being underneath all that. What is a Lunar after so long?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:17:02-07:00","id":103507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103503#post103503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be both plausible and thematic. I think I should clarify, though: when I said losing yourself in your power, I didn't mean going crazy with werewolf rage or just generally losing control. I meant losing your identity<br /> <br /> Lunars accomplish what they do, largely, by changing their shapes, including the shapes of their minds. All it takes to imagine a Lunar curse is to consider the effects of that. When you've transformed your own mind often enough, I expect you'll start to forget who you used to be, what you were like, what it was that made you believe the things you used to believe. Over their long millennia of continual change, I think it would be inevitable for Lunar Exalts to lose their human identities and simply stop being who and what they were. A mad Solar god-king may allow his virtue and perfection to consume him, but he's still a human being underneath all that. What is a Lunar after so long?</div> </div> </div> </div>Change of identity isn't really something you can enforce and model mechanically though. It's like you'd want to enforce character development. And no man can understand what a dog thinks, let alone a beetle. How exactly do you want to acomplish this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-01-2014, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:43:30-07:00","id":103524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103434#post103434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that the one where the world ends... but something not-so-shitty may or may not happen afterwards?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's the one from the W20 intro comic where the Garou and Fera can turn things around just as long as they don't give up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:45:58-07:00","id":103528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103507#post103507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change of identity isn't really something you can enforce and model mechanically though. It's like you'd want to enforce character development. And no man can understand what a dog thinks, let alone a beetle. How exactly do you want to acomplish this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've been thinking about it, actually:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103503#post103503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I should clarify, though: when I said losing yourself in your power, I didn't mean going crazy with werewolf rage or just generally losing control. I meant losing your identity<br /> <br /> Lunars accomplish what they do, largely, by changing their shapes, including the shapes of their minds. All it takes to imagine a Lunar curse is to consider the effects of that. When you've transformed your own mind often enough, I expect you'll start to forget who you used to be, what you were like, what it was that made you believe the things you used to believe. Over their long millennia of continual change, I think it would be inevitable for Lunar Exalts to lose their human identities and simply stop being who and what they were. A mad Solar god-king may allow his virtue and perfection to consume him, but he's still a human being underneath all that. What is a Lunar after so long?</div> </div> </div> </div>And it occurs to me, M\u00f8rke has said that animals in Third Edition will no longer just be wandering statblocks, but will have more unique characteristics. Maybe that includes mental characteristics. Maybe the more time you spend in a certain shape, the more you begin to manifest the characteristics of that shape in your inner nature.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a good justification for having a spirit shape? As more of a spirit guide, a way to find your way back to yourself? Because your spirit shape is, of course, the animal whose spirit you most embodied at the time you were Exalted. It could be used as a way of reattuning to yourself, restoring some of your identity. It's kind of thematic, since, in that case, the spirit shape would be to the Lunar almost what Gaia is to Luna herself, the spiritual anchor that keeps her bound to Creation so that she stays and protects it rather than flying off into the Wyld never to be heard from again.<br /> <br /> But maybe the spirit shape also changes over time, so in the end you're guaranteed to change. Or it gets harder to find your spirit shape. I dunno, it's something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:56:00-07:00","id":103535,"title":"","content":"That something is overthinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:55:33-07:00","id":103629,"title":"","content":"We've seen the writeup of the tyrant lizard. It didn't have anything in the way of that noted. Granted, that could change, but I'm betting not.<br /> <br /> Also,&quot;in danger of losing identity&quot; is something that I feel would probably be better being just Lilith's thing and not every Lunar's thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:21:55-07:00","id":103636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103471#post103471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I just don't see transformation is what they're really about. If Triumphant Howl of the Devil-Tiger had never been written, would we even be connecting them with the idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are, like, four shintai Charms in their original Manual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:54:52-07:00","id":103655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103636#post103636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are, like, four shintai Charms in their original Manual.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, there are three.<br /> <br /> Black Mirror Shintai, which comes from the Ebon Dragon, is more or less explicitly a lie achieved through sorcery and can be dispelled with countermagic... and only lets you change into a copy of someone else whom you hate, and changes your motivation to the opposite of theirs...<br /> <br /> And Soul-Sand Devil Shintai, which I think allows you to dematerialize permanently, and Scarlet Rapture Shintai, which lets you be <i>wind</i> for one action.<br /> <br /> Again, I know Infernals can change shape, I just don't think of it as really their core theme.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103629#post103629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've seen the writeup of the tyrant lizard. It didn't have anything in the way of that noted. Granted, that could change, but I'm betting not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd bet that too. Just speculating here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-01-2014, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:12:29-07:00","id":103662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103655#post103655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I know Infernals can change shape, I just don't think of it as really their core theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really need to be.<br /> <br /> All that matters is that Infernals can reasonably turn into a whole bunch of things that would seem silly for Lunars to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:17:48-07:00","id":103665,"title":"","content":"None of the above are things that Lunars can't already turn into in Second Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T16:52:25-07:00","id":103715,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I just have to double-post here, because that is such a bizarre statement. I mean, what do you mean <u>would</u> be silly? You know that already happens, right? Have you by chance had a look at the Lunar charmset?<ul><li><b>Luna's Hidden Face:</b> At Essence 3, take the form of any Wyld creature.</li> <li><b>Hearth-and-Flame Shell:</b> At Essence 4, take the form of any elemental. If applicable, your body is now made of electricity or wind or fire, with all the expected consequences.</li> <li><b>Green Sun Child:</b> At Essence 4, become any demon, any circle. Such as Ligier, provided you can kill and eat him first (edit: or taste his blood or have sex with him, if you have those Knacks).</li> <li><b>Hungry Dream Cloak</b>: At E4, become a Fair Folk. Learn Fair Folk Charms beginning at E5.</li> <li><b>Heart-Theft of the Behemoth:</b> At Essence 5, become any behemoth up to a certain size. At E7, become any behemoth of <u>any</u> size. Go to Thorns, drink Juggernaut's blood, become Juggernaut.</li> <li><b>Moon and Earth Song:</b> At E7, shapeshift into a mountain, a river, a forest, a desert or any other geographic feature, at a cost of 10 motes. Become immune to virtually any damage and oh right, you can still move.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I mean I like you a lot, Isator, really. You seem like someone it'd be nice to play with someday. But in your comments about Lunars on this and other threads, I have to wonder sometimes if you've really ever looked at Lunars. Stuff like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103461#post103461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that, when I think of something that shapeshifts in the same basic paradigm of therianthrope legends, and something that would shapeshift into, say, Angels from Evangelion, the idea of them both being the same thing feels kind of silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunars book actually references giant monster anime like Evangelion as a source of inspiration for Lunar games. You know the Knacks from DotFA/Glories explicitly allow your own spirit shape to be larger than a city, right? Larger than a city, and made of fire? You don't even need to eat anything's heart to do that. That's your own, true form.<br /> <br /> And you know you can use core Lunar Knacks like Hybrid Body Rearrangement (Essence 3) to mix various features of different shapes, so that instead of merely being a wolf of flame five miles long, you are now a dragon of flame five miles long, with eyes of lightning and claws of death-essence? Even at E5, you can take that form at a size large enough to engage armies in mass combat.<br /> <br /> It's just, it's not like these are obscure tricks... they're just the canon uses of Lunar powers. It's so weird to say it'd be silly to have Lunars shapeshift in ways like the Shintai charms allow. They <u>do</u> shapeshift like that. That's their power. There's nothing in the setting a Lunar can't already turn into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:23:23-07:00","id":103754,"title":"","content":"Form-taking doesn't grant you the form's supernatural powers, TSK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:30:19-07:00","id":103758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103754#post103754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Form-taking doesn't grant you the form's supernatural powers, TSK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it does, if you've also taken the knack for that! Essential Mirror Form for elementals, ghosts, gods, demons etc., and Shifting Wyld Tides for Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Not that you need many supernatural powers when you can crush an army by rolling over in your sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-01-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T00:19:01-07:00","id":103883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103528#post103528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I've been thinking about it, actually: And it occurs to me, M\u00f8rke has said that animals in Third Edition will no longer just be wandering statblocks, but will have more unique characteristics. Maybe that includes mental characteristics. Maybe the more time you spend in a certain shape, the more you begin to manifest the characteristics of that shape in your inner nature. Maybe this is a good justification for having a spirit shape? As more of a spirit guide, a way to find your way back to yourself? Because your spirit shape is, of course, the animal whose spirit you most embodied at the time you were Exalted. It could be used as a way of reattuning to yourself, restoring some of your identity. It's kind of thematic, since, in that case, the spirit shape would be to the Lunar almost what Gaia is to Luna herself. .../himself. But maybe the spirit shape also changes over time, so in the end you're guaranteed to change. Or it gets harder to resume your spirit shape. I dunno, it's something.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is very close to my headcanon even if I realize it'd be hard to accomplish mechanically. +1 to you sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T01:41:53-07:00","id":103911,"title":"","content":"Yes TSk, you're pretty much right, originally the intention behind Lunars was to have them have powers that would make Evangelion-style change possible. It was done so haphazardly and so badly that many people didn't even realize. And then Infernals pretty much did the same, except they did it right. Everybody forgot that, yes, originally in 2e Lunars were supposed to be able to do that. But that's not saying much, because what 2e Lunars were and what weren't supposed to do is lost in time and nobody can ever know, because their book really gives us no insight in the matter.<br /> <br /> Skip a few years, John and Holden came, with glowing halos, speaking words so sweet and seemingly wise, they spoke so matter-a-factly about what Lunars <i>aren't, </i>without ever once actually saying what they <i>are,</i> they talked about barbarian aesthetics with great conviction showing us all how it absolutely demands from Lunars a limitted ability to shapeshift, how shapshifting isn't really even their thing, but just one of their thing, not even the most important or definitive one, certainly not the one they are masters of and since, remember, it has to work with the barbarian vibe (everything has to, barbarian aesthetics is, after all, <b>the most important thing about Lunars and their definitive feature</b>), they should be able to change into a limitted suit of beings, dervied from legends and folklore John and Holden are interested in incorporating into Exalted. After all, you don't want to tell a story of your own, do you? Noooo, you want to retell the legends you know, surely! That will never get boring!<br /> <br /> And everybody pretty much bought it. Which, as long as it's executed right, is ok. But so many jimmies were rustled in the process that I wonder if it was worth it in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-02-2014, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T08:42:21-07:00","id":104069,"title":"","content":"Actually, a lot of what I just mentioned was published after Infernals, including the explicitly city-stomping powers from Glories - although Lunars have had other Knacks to do that since 2007.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about what Lunars originally were. I'm talking about what they are, presently, as of Exalted 2.5. It seems like every thread on this Exalt type has to be derailed into an argument by someone insisting that they can't do something they've actually <i>been</i> doing ever since their rulebook was published. Why is that?<br /> <br /> As for the current authors, what the've said has left me somewhat cautiously hopeful for third edition. It's a little like waiting while someone performs brain surgery on a friend, but in some ways, it sounds like what they have in mind might be closer to what my preferred reading of Lunars has been all along. The 'barbarian' stuff leaves me unsure, but that word is such a matter of interpretation it's never been applied accurately to anyone in the entire history of its use. So we'll just have to wait and see. As long as I can still go to the theater in Great Forks, I can probably handle being labeled a <i>political barbarian. W</i>hatever that turns out to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T09:52:33-07:00","id":104107,"title":"","content":"??? Sorry for more derailing, but I don't think anyone told us that Lunars will be political barbarians (that is people who live the barbarian lifestyle of nomadic tribes). The impression I got was that Lunars are stylistically barbarian because shapeshifting destroys your clothes, and relying on big cities could attract the attention of the Realm and Sidereals, and being self-reliant is a virtue in the Silver Pact and other stuff. Being a political barbarian is probably meaningless for anyone who has been Exalted for any period of time, because you're not really a part of society anymore. You might be leading it or whatever, but it's not the same anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1658-maelstromseeker","name":"maelstromseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:23:30-07:00","id":104128,"title":"","content":"Should not be feeding the further derail, especially since this is an interesting thread topic, on which I regrettably can't come up with anything to contribute. :/ Eh, just a quick dropping of links should be okay.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maelstromseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104107#post104107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">??? Sorry for more derailing, but I don't think anyone told us that Lunars will be political barbarians (that is people who live the barbarian lifestyle of nomadic tribes). The impression I got was that Lunars are stylistically barbarian because shapeshifting destroys your clothes, and relying on big cities could attract the attention of the Realm and Sidereals, and being self-reliant is a virtue in the Silver Pact and other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was a matter of mixing up the terms Holden had used in <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/413\" target=\"_blank\">his big ol' post on the topic</a> (thank you again, Nishkriya). Of which I would also be guilty, as I hadn't actually noticed until you mentioned it and I went to check. I don't think it's a big deal; it didn't sound like these are terms they plan to use in the future, just ones they used for the purposes of that discussion.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being a political barbarian is probably meaningless for anyone who has been Exalted for any period of time, because you're not really a part of society anymore. You might be leading it or whatever, but it's not the same anymore. </div> </div> </div>This is <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/417\" target=\"_blank\">broadly true</a>, though not necessarily the case. It may depend on what one considers &quot;part of society.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T11:23:04-07:00","id":104189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drecain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103883#post103883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is very close to my headcanon even if I realize it'd be hard to accomplish mechanically. +1 to you sir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I edited it the last part with some clarification. To restate, since it's now buried:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103528#post103528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it occurs to me, M\u00f8rke has said that animals in Third Edition will no longer just be wandering statblocks, but will have more unique characteristics. Maybe that includes mental characteristics. Maybe the more time you spend in a certain shape, the more you begin to manifest the characteristics of that shape in your inner nature.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a good justification for having a spirit shape? As more of a spirit guide, a way to find your way back to yourself? Because your spirit shape is, of course, the animal whose spirit you most embodied at the time you were Exalted. It could be used as a way of reattuning to yourself, restoring some of your identity. It's kind of thematic, since, in that case, the spirit shape would be to the Lunar almost what Gaia is to Luna herself, the spiritual anchor that keeps her bound to Creation so that she stays and protects it rather than flying off into the Wyld never to be heard from again.<br /> <br /> But maybe the spirit shape also changes over time, so in the end you're guaranteed to change. Or it gets harder to find your spirit shape. I dunno, it's something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having thought about it some more, there's a simpler way something like that could be implemented: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>In some general way, using your shapeshifting powers tend to gradually add to your Limit.</li> <li>At Limit Break, curse effects are modeled pretty much like they are now, except that instead of acting like your spirit shape, they compel you to act <u>unlike</u> your spirit shape. So if your spirit shape is a wolf, you might become disloyal or something.</li> <li>Optionally, every Limit Break also adds one dot to your <u>permanent</u> Limit, which in addition to chimeric effects could compound the existing curse, so you are now disloyal and selfish, two curses instead of one.</li> <li>In some general way, spending time in your spirit shape (or evoking it somehow) decreases your Limit and/or permanent Limit.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Seems simple enough. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T13:47:01-07:00","id":104317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104189#post104189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! I edited it the last part with some clarification. To restate, since it's now buried:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Having thought about it some more, there's a simpler way something like that could be implemented:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>In some general way, using your shapeshifting powers tend to gradually add to your Limit.</li> <li>At Limit Break, curse effects are modeled pretty much like they are now, except that instead of acting like your spirit shape, they compel you to act <u>unlike</u> your spirit shape. So if your spirit shape is a wolf, you might become disloyal or something.</li> <li>Optionally, every Limit Break also adds one dot to your <u>permanent</u> Limit, which in addition to chimeric effects could compound the existing curse, so you are now disloyal and selfish, two curses instead of one.</li> <li>In some general way, spending time in your spirit shape (or evoking it somehow) decreases your Limit and/or permanent Limit.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Seems simple enough. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrible. Punishing players for using their cool tools. Didn't we have enough of that with Abyssals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T13:57:23-07:00","id":104321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104069#post104069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, a lot of what I just mentioned was published after Infernals, including the explicitly city-stomping powers from Glories - although Lunars have had other Knacks to do that since 2007.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about what Lunars originally were. I'm talking about what they are, presently, as of Exalted 2.5. It seems like every thread on this Exalt type has to be derailed into an argument by someone insisting that they can't do something they've actually <i>been</i> doing ever since their rulebook was published. Why is that?<br /> <br /> As for the current authors, what the've said has left me somewhat cautiously hopeful for third edition. It's a little like waiting while someone performs brain surgery on a friend, but in some ways, it sounds like what they have in mind might be closer to what my preferred reading of Lunars has been all along. The 'barbarian' stuff leaves me unsure, but that word is such a matter of interpretation it's never been applied accurately to anyone in the entire history of its use. So we'll just have to wait and see. As long as I can still go to the theater in Great Forks, I can probably handle being labeled a <i>political barbarian. W</i>hatever that turns out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it was another bad rulebook. &quot;Better than Lunars 1e&quot; isn't a high hurdle, and it bumped into it on the way over with its V:tM-esque social interactions, tails of failure in the very thing that Lunars held onto for the hope of the future (half of the experiments that Lunars did with the TSR ended up blowing up in their faces), and number of Lunars that died doing something impressive, which the line then ran with. But hey, you can turn into blood apes. That's great, right?<br /> <br /> Well, no. Because having a tyrant lizard for a spirit shape mechanically overshadowed everything in a way reminiscent of 1E DBT. No one really learned anything, and then there was the &quot;real dice cap&quot; thing with Fury, Spirit, and Genius that kind of just dropped you in the middle of nowhere and said, &quot;There might be a theme. Go and find it.&quot; Which is not a very fun thing for Exalted that are supposed to come with a narrower theme to have in their book.<br /> <br /> In essence, they aren't what's presented in the book, and were never meant to be. Second edition didn't open vast opportunities, it stretched them further than they had substance to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:26:12-07:00","id":104338,"title":"","content":"I guess a tyrant lizard overshadows everything if you're not being very creative, sure. But all it takes is a few knacks to have your default DBT be <i>carapace of living diamond surrounded by tentacles of electricity</i> straight out of chargen. If you don't want to grab and shock the tyrant lizard with your electro-tentacles, you can reflexively decide that they're fire tentacles instead, or shift them into toxic T-1000 stabbing weapons and rip and tear the tyrant lizard, or a thousand other possibilities I for one find a lot more fun and effective than tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> But this thread is not about the alleged shortcomings of Lunar shapeshifting/thematics/anything. If you want to start a thread about that, go ahead. Otherwise, do you have anything to say on-topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:45:21-07:00","id":104353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104338#post104338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess a tyrant lizard overshadows everything if you're not being very creative, sure. But all it takes is a few knacks to have your default DBT be <i>carapace of living diamond surrounded by tentacles of electricity</i> straight out of chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, by the rules as written, that's nothing more than an extra 6L/6B. With CotSM and ridiculous dice adder caps, the tyrant lizard Lunar wouldn't just open that up like a can-opener, that would be a case of pink crystalline mist.<br /> <br /> But here's the better question - how is being a carapace of diamond with electrical arc tentacles representative of being a fusion of beast and human, hero and monster? How does it follow from the game that they were based on? None of the other splats ever gets their links to the inspirational WoD game called into question like Lunars. I think it may have something to do with people not liking Werewolf trying to scour every last call-out of it from Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't want to grab and shock the tyrant lizard with your electro-tentacles, you can reflexively decide that they're fire tentacles instead, or shift them into toxic T-1000 stabbing weapons and rip and tear the tyrant lizard, or a thousand other possibilities I for one find a lot more fun and effective than tyrant lizard. </div> </div> </div>You can only do what the rules say that you can, and the rules say &quot;One hit, the tyrant lizard rips the other guy apart and kills him.&quot; Especially before CotSM was trimmed back, so you'd have diamond wonder having to soak something on the order of 45-60L.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this thread is not about the alleged shortcomings of Lunar shapeshifting/thematics/anything. If you want to start a thread about that, go ahead. Otherwise, do you have anything to say on-topic? </div> </div> </div>It was your tangent to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T15:43:28-07:00","id":104382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103524#post103524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's the one from the W20 intro comic where the Garou and Fera can turn things around just as long as they don't give up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen that specific comic and am not sure what its original source is so I can't look it up.<br /> <br /> The outlook of W:tA has always been very bleak though. The idea that the Garou weren't going to save the world always struck me as a central premise. You could be awesome. You could kick ass. You could win renown and everyone could respect you. Ultimately though, the world had already hit cascade failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T15:48:19-07:00","id":104386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104382#post104382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never seen that specific comic and am not sure what its original source is so I can't look it up.<br /> <br /> The outlook of W:tA has always been very bleak though. The idea that the Garou weren't going to save the world always struck me as a central premise. You could be awesome. You could kick ass. You could win renown and everyone could respect you. Ultimately though, the world had already hit cascade failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the bleak, the-end-is-happening time of Revised edition, yes. For the 20th anniversary edition, they cut the terminator line back, so it can be a not completely bleak celebration of the game's history and themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T15:53:09-07:00","id":104392,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: The Maybe-not-olypse. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:01:01-07:00","id":104400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104392#post104392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: The Maybe-not-olypse. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, there's still that looming. It's just that you can try to mend the mistakes of the past. And if you did, you could get the world back on track. The Apocalypse isn't even a guaranteed end, anyway - all the fighting is to determine the shape of the aftermath.<br /> <br /> But damn if the world isn't really, really messed up. Every moment adds more work. You'll have to work smart and hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:24:50-07:00","id":104423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104321#post104321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it was another bad rulebook. &quot;Better than Lunars 1e&quot; isn't a high hurdle, and it bumped into it on the way over with its V:tM-esque social interactions, tails of failure in the very thing that Lunars held onto for the hope of the future (half of the experiments that Lunars did with the TSR ended up blowing up in their faces), and number of Lunars that died doing something impressive, which the line then ran with. But hey, you can turn into blood apes. That's great, right?<br /> <br /> Well, no. Because having a tyrant lizard for a spirit shape mechanically overshadowed everything in a way reminiscent of 1E DBT. No one really learned anything, and then there was the &quot;real dice cap&quot; thing with Fury, Spirit, and Genius that kind of just dropped you in the middle of nowhere and said, &quot;There might be a theme. Go and find it.&quot; Which is not a very fun thing for Exalted that are supposed to come with a narrower theme to have in their book.<br /> <br /> In essence, they aren't what's presented in the book, and were never meant to be. Second edition didn't open vast opportunities, it stretched them further than they had substance to offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I did actually miss the fact that you were replying to a question I\u2019d asked here, which was kind of buried in the quote itself, and that you were talking about the pre-errata version. You're right, it did have issues, and that probably is why there seems to be such confusion about Lunar abilities. I guess I was reacting to the idea that tyrant lizard makes Lunars unplayable. I mean I'd never have allowed a player to have a tyrant lizard as his spirit shape in the first place, nor been allowed to, so that was never really a game-breaking issue for me.<br /> <br /> It's probably also the presentation of things. In Infernals and Broken-Winged Crane, every shapechanging charm is accompanied by like half a page of elaborate descriptive text of how awesome the PC's transformation is. Lunars just says, like, &quot;The Lunar may now become a behemoth,&quot; and then walks off. So yeah, that happened.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I kind of prefer it the second way. I don't need to feel like I'm being flattered by the charm descriptions. But it doesn't exactly help emphasize some things that are kind of important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:42:28-07:00","id":104429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104423#post104423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I did actually miss the fact that you were replying to a question I\u2019d asked here, which was kind of buried in the quote itself, and that you were talking about the pre-errata version. You're right, it did have issues, and that probably is why there seems to be such confusion about Lunar abilities. I guess I was reacting to the idea that tyrant lizard makes Lunars unplayable. I mean I'd never have allowed a player to have a tyrant lizard as his spirit shape in the first place, nor been allowed to, so that was never really a game-breaking issue for me.<br /> <br /> It's probably also the presentation of things. In Infernals and Broken-Winged Crane, every shapechanging charm is accompanied by like half a page of elaborate descriptive text of how awesome the PC's transformation is. Lunars just says, like, &quot;The Lunar may now become a behemoth,&quot; and then walks off. So yeah, that happened.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I kind of prefer it the second way. I don't need to feel like I'm being flattered by the charm descriptions. But it doesn't exactly help emphasize some things that are kind of important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even post-errata, the spirit shape still expands dice caps to a ludicrous, optimizing degree. You're still looking at a base damage value of 33L. You could prevent people from taking that as a spirit shape, but that's not really much of a fix, nor is it resolving the issue. It's also frustrating to deny the thematic space that Lunars do have, which the tyrant lizard would certainly be a part of, in favor of pretty much everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:13:45-07:00","id":104444,"title":"","content":"Well, that's where a good storyteller comes in. I wouldn't approve tyrant lizard as a spirit shape, because I don't like to get the idea that players are treating their characters as pure statblocks, but I have nothing against PCs acquiring the shape ingame. That said, I'm not going to ignore the obvious problems of that shape. For one thing, good luck going anywhere indoors. For another, trying to win a clinch roll with arms that can't even reach the middle of your torso, when your opponent is composed of raw electricity for instance, is probably not a good idea. Especially since your opponent can just banish the tentacles reflexively if s/he loses.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm guessing you got your 6B/6L stats for diamond exoskeleton from the <i>stone body</i> mutation. Stone is generally a poor substitute for diamond. You can only use the rules as written, yes, but the rules say you're meant to be coming up with your own mutations when appropriate, not just relying on what you find in setting books. For that matter, even though the text for Hearth-and-Flame Shell does say that your raw elemental essence will cause damage to those it comes in contact with when you're using an elemental shape, it doesn't actually give any stats for that damage or any other effects. The ST has to fill that out too.<br /> <br /> You're right that it's lacking a lot of substance in that regard. A lot of things in Exalted are like that, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104429#post104429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also frustrating to deny the thematic space that Lunars do have, which the tyrant lizard would certainly be a part of, in favor of pretty much everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anyone seriously ever chosen tyrant lizard for thematic reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:25:08-07:00","id":104454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104338#post104338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But all it takes is a few knacks to have your default DBT be <i>carapace of living diamond surrounded by tentacles of electricity</i> straight out of chargen. If you don't want to grab and shock the tyrant lizard with your electro-tentacles, you can reflexively decide that they're fire tentacles instead, or shift them into toxic T-1000 stabbing weapons and rip and tear the tyrant lizard, or a thousand other possibilities I for one find a lot more fun and effective than tyrant lizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just me, but another reason I'm repelled by this for Lunars is that it feels less like a natural extension of or addition to their themes, and more like an attempt at gonzo one-upmanship; to try and take the tradition of animalistic shapeshifting and make it kewler by going in for a lot more elaborate adjectives.<br /> <br /> It's just more T-Rexes and F-16s; sound and fury, signifying nothing.<br /> <br /> Mind, people did this with Infernals as well, and still do somewhat. I'm <i>more</i> okay with Green Sun Princes having carapaces of diamond and electricity tentacles (I mean, that's pretty She Who Lives in Her Name as it is), but it should probably stop about there, lest the actual Exalt become crushed under the weight of all their extraneous additions.<br /> <br /> I dislike the idea of Exalts becoming Warhammer 40,000 protagonists, is what I'm getting at.<br /> <br /> That last line in particular is something I balk at: Lunars should not be written with an assumption that people who turn into animals, or have other powers related to that general theme, are less interesting than people who turn into other stuff, because Lunars are based on the literature and mythology of primal gods and animalistic shapeshifters. They should be written to appeal to what people love about that stuff, what makes it enduring, not assume that nobody cares and then add a bunch of bells and whistles on.<br /> <br /> Lunar shapeshifting is like daiklaves in that regard.<br /> <br /> Except daiklaves never had two Editions worth of books actually assuming that people didn't like them at all, and trying to apologise for it.<br /> <br /> Lunars have a bad enough track record as it is, between a hardback that all but said &quot;we know this is terrible, but here's some ideas that might help you have fun anyway&quot; and a follow up that said &quot;we know the last one was terrible, so here's stuff to make them act and function more like Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> They've one strike left, they shouldn't be swinging it at &quot;we know animalistic shapeshifting is boring, so here's turning into a random mess of features instead&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:26:20-07:00","id":104457,"title":"","content":"More broadly, this is a sterling example of why you shouldn't tie such a vital facet of gameplay (dice caps) to a seemingly-innocuous choice made and set in stone at chargen (Spirit Shape).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:27:37-07:00","id":104460,"title":"","content":"Right now, I'm looking at this thread, and all the others like it, and I wonder if how the idea for Third Edition Lunars having an inner struggle to define who they are and what they're for isn't one big laugh.<br /> <br /> Appropriate, though. When time comes to play a Lunar, I'll definitely have a lot of practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:30:22-07:00","id":104464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104460#post104460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, I'm looking at this thread, and all the others like it, and I wonder if how the idea for Third Edition Lunars having an inner struggle to define who they are and what they're for isn't one big laugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a cute bit of meta-humor, whether coincidental or deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:32:02-07:00","id":104465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104457#post104457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More broadly, this is a sterling example of why you shouldn't tie such a vital facet of gameplay (dice caps) to a seemingly-innocuous choice made and set in stone at chargen (Spirit Shape).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Castes are similar, in that they are an unchangeable choice that has a major mechanical impact.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure that the developers, as they work on making the Totem more important, are also working on making it seem exactly as important as it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:32:08-07:00","id":104466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104454#post104454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's just me, but another reason I'm repelled by this for Lunars is that it feels less like a natural extension of or addition to their themes, and more like an attempt at gonzo one-upmanship; to try and take the tradition of animalistic shapeshifting and make it kewler by going in for a lot more elaborate adjectives.<br /> <br /> It's just more T-Rexes and F-16s; sound and fury, signifying nothing.<br /> <br /> Mind, people did this with Infernals as well, and still do somewhat. I'm <i>more</i> okay with Green Sun Princes having carapaces of diamond and electricity tentacles (I mean, that's pretty She Who Lives in Her Name as it is), but it should probably stop about there, lest the actual Exalt become crushed under the weight of all their extraneous additions.<br /> <br /> I dislike the idea of Exalts becoming Warhammer 40,000 protagonists, is what I'm getting at.<br /> <br /> That last line in particular is something I balk at: Lunars should not be written with an assumption that people who turn into animals, or have other powers related to that general theme, are less interesting than people who turn into other stuff, because Lunars are based on the literature and mythology of primal gods and animalistic shapeshifters. They should be written to appeal to what people love about that stuff, what makes it enduring, not assume that nobody cares and then add a bunch of bells and whistles on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, this is just such a bizarre complaint. Since when has Lunar shapeshifting ever been limited to animal shapes? You get so many ridiculous charms in MOEP Lunars alone to turn yourself into crazy things, to define 2e Lunar themes as excluding non-animal things seems like saying, &quot;Maybe it's me, but I really don't see sneaking around and using larceny as part of the theme of Night Caste Solars.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:42:07-07:00","id":104476,"title":"","content":"You know why they put those Knacks in there?<br /> <br /> Because people in 1E bitched about being 'just' animals when the Alchemicals were Transformers, and everyone else seemed to be edging in on the transformation niche.<br /> <br /> They are <i>terrible</i> for what they thought they had to do, and trying to justify anything based off of them is starting on very shaky ground, sad to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:52:47-07:00","id":104488,"title":"","content":"Now, in fairness, Lunars <i>should</i> have powers that let them turn into demons and monsters that <i>exist</i>.<br /> <br /> You know, after eating them. Or occasionally having sex with them, possibly even after beating them in some kind of contest.<br /> <br /> Primal god mythology is brimming with creatures and people that steal faces and skins. Being able to turn into an electric diamond mollusc, well, that's just Exalted having a wider variety of faces to steal than most mythology.<br /> <br /> But the key is, you tore it off the person who naturally had it and are wearing it on the outside of yourself. The quality to do so is part of Lunar Essence, but the thing itself is not; not the way that turning into a beast or certain variety of other personal transformations is. Not the way turning into a lotus of brass and bile sitting upon a looping river of water so pure that it burns the ugly world it touches is a thing for an Infernal to turn into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:57:46-07:00","id":104489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104488#post104488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the key is, you tore it off the person who naturally had it and are wearing it on the outside of yourself. The quality to do so is part of Lunar Essence, but the thing itself is not; not the way that turning into a beast or certain variety of other personal transformations is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think that's missing the point entirely. Shapes are not something you wear, they're something you <i>become.</i> You didn't just tear something's arm of and stick it on yourself; you absorbed its essence into your own and internalized its shape, after which you shape yourself into it. It's not something outside of you; it is you. It is made of your essence. Every Lunar transformation is a personal transformation. That's kind of the whole point, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:16:48-07:00","id":104494,"title":"","content":"Which leads to the question then: What use is the base Lunar if all they do is become other things, then mix and match them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:27:30-07:00","id":104502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104454#post104454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *snip*.</div> </div> </div> </div>The focus on animalistic shapeshifting isn't where they're going with Lunars as the core theme, I believe it's been said that the link between Lunars and animals comes from the link between Luna and Gaia. Their themes are of shapeshifter mythology, so that can range from animalistic were-hyena legends to Cuchulain.<br /> <br /> I personally like how Lunars can turn an enemies shapes against them and combine shapes into their own things. It wasn't Solars fighting Behemoths in the First Age, for they were an enemy of immense size. As the Solar's combatted demons of a more human stature, it was the Lunars, greater than giants, turning the enemies weapons against them in climatic battle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:31:42-07:00","id":104504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104494#post104494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leads to the question then: What use is the base Lunar if all they do is become other things, then mix and match them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave an answer to that in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103528#post103528\">this</a> post. That's the best I've got so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104502#post104502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The focus on animalistic shapeshifting isn't where they're going with Lunars as the core theme, I believe it's been said that the link between Lunars and animals comes from the link between Luna and Gaia. Their themes are of shapeshifter mythology, so that can range from animalistic were-hyena legends to Cuchulain.<br /> <br /> I personally like how Lunars can turn an enemies shapes against them and combine shapes into their own things. It wasn't Solars fighting Behemoths in the First Age, for they were an enemy of immense size. As the Solar's combatted demons of a more human stature, it was the Lunars, greater than giants, turning the enemies weapons against them in climatic battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, he gets it. I mean what else in this setting can become a hekatonkhire as a reflexive action? You need us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:38:19-07:00","id":104508,"title":"","content":"Why?<br /> <br /> No, this is a serious question: Why is being everything but you, something to hang your hat on as your primary schtick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:38:36-07:00","id":104509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104444#post104444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's where a good storyteller comes in. I wouldn't approve tyrant lizard as a spirit shape, because I don't like to get the idea that players are treating their characters as pure statblocks, but I have nothing against PCs acquiring the shape ingame.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't put spirit shapes off. They're totemic to a character. You have them from the moment of Exaltation, like your anima banner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I'm not going to ignore the obvious problems of that shape. For one thing, good luck going anywhere indoors. For another, trying to win a clinch roll with arms that can't even reach the middle of your torso, when your opponent is composed of raw electricity for instance, is probably not a good idea. Especially since your opponent can just banish the tentacles reflexively if s/he loses. </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be likely to come to that. The formless not-Lunar would die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'm guessing you got your 6B/6L stats for diamond exoskeleton from the <i>stone body</i> mutation. Stone is generally a poor substitute for diamond. </div> </div> </div>I think that you need to read the text of the mutation again. It mentioned crystal lattices as an option, just like how flight can net you wings or a helium bladder for LTA static lift, or any number of other possibilities.<br /> <br /> Also, given the use of a large, heavy hammer, diamond's vaunted hardness doesn't really pay off too well, as with extreme hardness comes extreme brittleness. In spite of the JJBA series 4 title, you can rest assured that diamond is not actually unbreakable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has anyone seriously ever chosen tyrant lizard for thematic reasons? </div> </div> </div>There are an awful lot of options for it. The name itself, for Lunars who were autocrats prior to their Second Breath. It might be the greatest terror of the character's homeland. The character could be a great hunter with keen eyesight and smell, and utilize ambushes to bring prey to her. You could have a mystic that chews on bones to gain insights. It's not really confining for any reason. Great terrors, aka northern titans, weren't, either. It was probably more common in 1e, when the only Strength-adder took 15 turns to warm up and lasted for maybe half that. And was based off of Charisma, with a Manipulation Charm as its prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:42:34-07:00","id":104513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103353#post103353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Night Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first Exalted character was a Night Caste, and honestly I alwasy felt not like I was subtle or sneaky, but that I was beating people around the head with my stealth charms until they couldn't take it anymore. I think the worst time was using perfect pickpocket technique. I turned in a set of keys to various super-secret things in Lookshy to get them to like me. I then stole it back from them as they were leaving (I was in prison at the time, long story). The guards, not being stupid, came back and searched me again, but I planted them on one of the guards until they were done, and then stole it back again. That's not really subtle or tricksy or dexterous, since I was using a perfect successes charm to do it with. I literally beat them around the head with massive Solar power until they couldn't handle it any more.<br /> <br /> There was also the time an elder Sidereal wanted to steal something from us, planned everything out, teleported in, beat the snot out of us, grabbed the bag the McGuffin was in, and tried to teleport away (actually the super long mountain to mountain jump thing they had). I, being a Night Caste Solar was all like 'There is nothing you can steal that I can't take away', and just stole the thing while he was trouncing our Twilight. He leaps away, having totally schooled us, with the bag, but not with the super secret nifty trinket. Literally, the fight was 'You can be better than us, plan more than us, know everything that is going on, understand what you are getting into, and utterly overwhelm us, but we're still Solars.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:43:17-07:00","id":104516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104466#post104466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again, this is just such a bizarre complaint. Since when has Lunar shapeshifting ever been limited to animal shapes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in first edition (NB: humans are animals, albeit not ones that serve as totemic shapes. At least, not for Lunars.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You get so many ridiculous charms in MOEP Lunars alone to turn yourself into crazy things, to define 2e Lunar themes as excluding non-animal things seems like saying, &quot;Maybe it's me, but I really don't see sneaking around and using larceny as part of the theme of Night Caste Solars.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That doesn't follow at all. There's nothing entitling the concept of Lunars, being werewolf Exalted, to non-animal shapes, and Lunars aren't supposed to cover every base in painstaking detail and power listings like Solars do. Above all, they're shapeshifters in the vein of shamanic spirit-talkers and tricksters of myth, as well as the monstrous beasts of legend. Dragon-Blooded cover elementals pretty well, even if 2e only let them merge with them, Infernals have the demon side cornered, and other character types can pick up other shapeshifting concepts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:52:41-07:00","id":104520,"title":"","content":"Ahhh yes, I remember now.<br /> <br /> I remember <a href=\"http://hellsing.wikia.com/wiki/The_Captain\" target=\"_blank\">the Captain</a>.<br /> <br /> Much of what I want from Lunars is in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T19:02:30-07:00","id":104523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104508#post104508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?<br /> <br /> No, this is a serious question: Why is being everything but you, something to hang your hat on as your primary schtick?</div> </div> </div> </div>For two main reasons: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Because, as Godjaw said, it's completely necessary.</li> <li>Because it's fun.</li> </ol><br /> And yeah, that was a completely serious answer. Luna is a god/dess of infinite forms, and every form is true. His/her chosen change and adapt themselves for the same reasons s/he does: for the sake of others and because to do so is their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-02-2014, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T20:41:00-07:00","id":104562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104460#post104460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, I'm looking at this thread, and all the others like it, and I wonder if how the idea for Third Edition Lunars having an inner struggle to define who they are and what they're for isn't one big laugh.<br /> <br /> Appropriate, though. <u>When time comes to play a Lunar, I'll definitely have a lot of practice.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute. So you haven't actually played one, ever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T22:53:12-07:00","id":104622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104454#post104454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last line in particular is something I balk at: Lunars should not be written with an assumption that people who turn into animals, or have other powers related to that general theme, are less interesting than people who turn into other stuff, because Lunars are based on the literature and mythology of primal gods and animalistic shapeshifters. They should be written to appeal to what people love about that stuff, what makes it enduring, not assume that nobody cares and then add a bunch of bells and whistles on.<br /> <br /> Lunar shapeshifting is like daiklaves in that regard.<br /> <br /> Except daiklaves never had two Editions worth of books actually assuming that people didn't like them at all, and trying to apologise for it.<br /> <br /> Lunars have a bad enough track record as it is, between a hardback that all but said &quot;we know this is terrible, but here's some ideas that might help you have fun anyway&quot; and a follow up that said &quot;we know the last one was terrible, so here's stuff to make them act and function more like Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> They've one strike left, they shouldn't be swinging it at &quot;we know animalistic shapeshifting is boring, so here's turning into a random mess of features instead&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I thought we has a massive disagreement over it... but I agree with all of this. Lunars embody classic, simple themes, and beasts are part of it. Much like Solars making the human be fucking awesome, Lunars should make being a beast be fucking awesome, and not some second-rate prize. They are the tigers that hunted and devoured the Primordials, and being a big vortex of ten thousand limbs wearing the Lunar's face just means you're more exotic food.<br /> <br /> Lunars are also the Moon, Moonlight, Lunacy, Madness, and Chaos (and tied to the Wyld, which in my view should be signaled with Charms that tie to it as Sidereals do Heaven, and Abyssals to the Underworld), so I do expect it could be the form of a tiger whose stripes exhude moonlight, whose eyes pour out with essence and whose jaws are adamant... but it'd still be a goddamn tiger. (EDIT: Or the fluid, shimmering, wolf-but-unreal-wolf, fluid, size-changing fighting style of The Captain, yes!)<br /> <br /> That should be protected and be awesome. And yet...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104508#post104508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?<br /> <br /> No, this is a serious question: Why is being everything but you, something to hang your hat on as your primary schtick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because defeating an enemy and getting his weapons/form is incredibly fun? It's the core mechanic in several videogames (Devil May Cry has you getting demon-forms, for instance) for a reason, and possessing a good way to use 'enemy skill' would be great as an alternative to your own warform. I hope the 3e team seeds the sort of traits they give to animals around to Demons and Gods, so their SHAPE is awesome without the need to get their Charms for it to matter. Historically Lunars has made turning into another shape weak, when Shape-collecting should be a very interesting and engaging minigame.<br /> <br /> (And having an array of [awesome, stolen] battle-forms should be a good alternative to embodying your totem.)<br /> <br /> (And I think I'm the only one who thinks that Totem is a far more engaging word than Spirit Shape, but so there.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T02:07:55-07:00","id":104713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104508#post104508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?<br /> <br /> No, this is a serious question: Why is being everything but you, something to hang your hat on as your primary schtick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's more interesting than being a Silver Solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T02:11:11-07:00","id":104715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104502#post104502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their themes are of shapeshifter mythology, so that can range from animalistic were-hyena legends to Cuchulain.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but notably not Alex Mercer or John Carpenter's the Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T02:18:33-07:00","id":104717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104489#post104489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just think that's missing the point entirely. Shapes are not something you wear, they're something you <i>become.</i> You didn't just tear something's arm of and stick it on yourself; you absorbed its essence into your own and internalized its shape, after which you shape yourself into it. It's not something outside of you; it is you. It is made of your essence. Every Lunar transformation is a personal transformation. That's kind of the whole point, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're misunderstanding what I mean when I say &quot;wearing somebody else's face&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yes, you're transforming into them. You're doing do because you killed them and drank their blood. <i>That</i> part is the Lunar quality in the equation; it's not about what you turn into, but why you're able to. As surely as the Infernal transformations because they've cultivated a series of physical and spiritual demonic mutations.<br /> <br /> That a Lunar can turn into demonic monsters does not resonate throughout their Charms, but that Lunars turn into things by killing them and eating their heart does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T02:38:40-07:00","id":104726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104715#post104715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but notably not Alex Mercer or John Carpenter's the Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how do you represent this difference mechanically?<br /> <br /> More to the point, what IS the difference really, except that one of those sources Holden and John recognize as a good one to base Lunars on and the other not?<br /> <br /> If the development process here is to just find some sources and than try to base Lunars on those sources, instead of finding coherent concept for their powers, than they're gonna end up just as jumbled and incoherent as they have in 1 and 2 edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-03-2014, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T02:49:57-07:00","id":104730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104726#post104726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how do you represent this difference mechanically?<br /> <br /> More to the point, what IS the difference really, except that one of those sources Holden and John recognize as a good one to base Lunars on and the other not?<br /> <br /> If the development process here is to just find some sources and than try to base Lunars on those sources, instead of finding coherent concept for their powers , than their gonna end up just as jumbled and incoherent as they have in 1 and 2 edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because those two are represented in Exalted through Infernal in 3rd Edition, squick-shifting are their schtick now ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T03:31:32-07:00","id":104741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104730#post104730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because those two are represented in Exalted through Infernal in 3rd Edition, squick-shifting are their schtick now ;D</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, how do you tell the difference? How do you make that difference meaningful? How do you avoid the &quot;Infernals are better Lunars than Lunars problem&quot;?<br /> <br /> See, that's why I am uncertain about this &quot;corrupted Solars&quot; thing. It's shallow. Too shallow to carry the splat. But Infernals have demonic realm and it's a subsetting established enough to draw a lot from it. Infernals can stand on their own by being demonic Exalts alone.<br /> <br /> Now, can Lunars stand on their own by being shapeshifting barbarian silver Solars? I have my doubts about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-03-2014, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T05:11:53-07:00","id":104765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104726#post104726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how do you represent this difference mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that, in the whole wide range of impressive custom attacks and Merits that animals will have to represent their capabilities, there will be things that would make sense for a diamond carapace electric tentacle monster that won't really fit in at all, so that's a start.<br /> <br /> I honestly have very little idea of what Lunars' non-shapeshifting powers will be like (to the extent that powers that just don't happen to be &quot;turn into an animal&quot; are such), in mechanics or concept, but I know what I want, I know it's what the developers are gunning for, and I know that almost everything I've seen them bring out, especially with the previews for the new Edition, is a fairly well-realised mechanical representation of an underlying concept, so I trust in their expertise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">More to the point, what IS the difference really, except that one of those sources Holden and John recognize as a good one to base Lunars on and the other not?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, while I'm sure that there are some areas in which differences in shapeshifting really do have meaningful mechanical distinctions, I do think there's also something to be said for how sometimes a minor mechanical difference with a larger aesthetic modification saying a lot for different Exalted being different, and the greater implications people draw thereof.<br /> <br /> The difference between Fire and Stones Strike and Green Sun Nimbus Flare is fairly minor in mechanics, but in character one of them is exceptional skill with a sword (with a bit of Solar Essence put in its edge by such), and the other is wreathing an attack in toxic green flame, and these give different perspectives on what the character behind the powers is.<br /> <br /> Lunars being presented as primal shapeshifter heroes rather than protean alien monsters creates different priorities in who they are and what they do, and that has its importance.<br /> <br /> (I'd also assume that, like Green Sun Nimbus Flare, it might also mean that their Charm cascades evolve differently, but that's a level of technical expertise that is quite beyond me)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the development process here is to just find some sources and than try to base Lunars on those sources, instead of finding coherent concept for their powers, than they're gonna end up just as jumbled and incoherent as they have in 1 and 2 edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming that finding similar sources does not already lend itself to coherent concepts, but Solars already remonstrate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T05:23:26-07:00","id":104772,"title":"","content":"There is a grand canyon worth of distance between &quot;assuming turning into animals is boring&quot; and &quot;wanting more than just turning into animals.&quot; One of the things I'm actually most excited about is making animal forms matter more, but if that change comes at the expense of being able to make a lunar that turns into various mythic god-monsters I'm going to be pissed. Both elements are things I think are crucial elements of Lunars. <br /> <br /> Now as for the Totem and being locked in by your initial choice, I would actually like to see the ability to pick up additional Totems as time goes on. After all, many of the gods this spirit form idea seems to be modelled on have more than one associated animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T05:58:07-07:00","id":104782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104765#post104765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're assuming that finding similar sources does not already lend itself to coherent concepts, but Solars already remonstrate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, the design philosophy of Solars is not &quot;give them Achilles powers, give them Hercules powers, etc&quot;. The idea is to give them abilities that let players create characters inspired by those legends, but which are unique. Lunar paradigm seems to be &quot;we're just gonna make &lt;specific legend&gt; inspired power and give it to players&quot;. And that has never been satisfying, because there is no coherent theme behind it.<br /> <br /> And aesthetics alone isn't nearly enough to carry Lunars into the new eidition, especially when barbarian aethetics will heavily overlap with Solar characters. This overlap will always work to the detriment of Lunars, because let's be honest, being a barbarian god-king is still going to be more satisfying as a Solar, than as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> If the extent of Lunar coherence is &quot;barbarian aesthetics + specific powers inspired by specific legends&quot; than no, that's just not enough to make them lasting. A novelty at first, when they come out, perhaps. But they will get boring very quickly. Which, to be fair, might be the point, we wouldn't want them to still be popular at the tables when Infernals come out right?<br /> <br /> Recently I've worked my way through Niksha-can't remember the name-yia to see Devs quotes on Lunars. And one thing common I can see, is that not once have they ever said when they think Lunars are supposed to be. The <i>only</i> time any information was given, was when Holden said that they are &quot;untamed, unbowed Exalted&quot;. You'll note that that's extremly criptic, bordering on meaningless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104765#post104765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that, in the whole wide range of impressive custom attacks and Merits that animals will have to represent their capabilities, there will be things that would make sense for a diamond carapace electric tentacle monster that won't really fit in at all, so that's a start.<br /> <br /> I honestly have very little idea of what Lunars' non-shapeshifting powers will be like (to the extent that powers that just don't happen to be &quot;turn into an animal&quot; are such), in mechanics or concept, but I know what I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOk, what do you want? What do you want these non-shapeshifting powers to be like? What sort of coherent theme do you want them to have, how are they suppsed to look visually, how are they supposed to work with setting's metaphysics?<br /> <br /> Exactly what do you know about Lunars beyond &quot;they can turn into animals and sometimes other things I guess&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-03-2014, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T06:01:09-07:00","id":104783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104717#post104717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're misunderstanding what I mean when I say &quot;wearing somebody else's face&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yes, you're transforming into them. You're doing do because you killed them and drank their blood. <i>That</i> part is the Lunar quality in the equation; it's not about what you turn into, but why you're able to. As surely as the Infernal transformations because they've cultivated a series of physical and spiritual demonic mutations.<br /> <br /> That a Lunar can turn into demonic monsters does not resonate throughout their Charms, but that Lunars turn into things by killing them and eating their heart does.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, you're not answering my question. You've never actually played a Lunar, have you? So I mean, earlier in the thread, when you said that Infernals could turn into a whole bunch of things Lunars couldn't turn into, and I said that was crazy and asked if you'd ever read the Lunar charmset... the answer was no, right? You hadn't read it?<br /> <br /> If so, I think what you're missing is the key ability of Lunars to not just change themselves, but to change only parts of themselves. When the hypothetical No Moon is shadowing someone, he might use HBR to reflexively produce the <i>chameleon</i> mutation, and the <i>wall walking</i> mutation. Wary of a trap, he produces the <i>sonar</i> mutation and <i>shark sight</i> mutation and suddenly notices the invisible Night Caste sneaking up behind him. And yeah, in the case of melee, he may well reflexively transmute his coyote DBT form into a coyote of black crystal, grab the Night Caste with one or more tentacles of electricity, produce a couple of blade-arms, shift into a crystal strix and fly away or all of the above, because those are all things even starting Lunars do.<br /> <br /> Please no quibbling with the mechanics of who would come out on top in the hypothetical encounter this time, because that's not important. The point is that Lunars accomplish whatever they do by adapting themselves. Not only is that the basis of their amazing powers, it's their very nature. It's not because &quot;animals are boring.&quot; It's just because there's a whole lot in the universe in addition to animals and Lunars do not limit themselves to just a few options; they can be anything that exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-03-2014, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:08:20-07:00","id":104825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104715#post104715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but notably not Alex Mercer or John Carpenter's the Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure a lot of people will think this is a good comment, but in reality it's the complete opposite of the truth. In the entire 2nd Edition setting, there is really nothing more like <i>The Thing</i> than a Lunar. And a chimeric Lunar goes far beyond that.<br /> <br /> But you'll probably never know that unless you actually play one, because in all the illustrations and comics throughout the books, you never once see one of their more impressive shapeshifting abilities at work. Not even the charm-based ones like Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace. Once in a while, you'll see a Lunar drawn with a couple of extra mutations; for the most part, they just look like either animalistic humans or their default DBT forms. And it's very sad.<br /> <br /> It's sad because not only can Lunars be <i>The Thing,</i> it's practically their core mechanic. With the possible exception of DBT/Fury, Hybrid Body Rearranegment is probably the most useful power a Lunar will ever have. And yeah, the most fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:53:49-07:00","id":104853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104825#post104825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the entire 2nd Edition setting, there is really nothing more like <i>The Thing</i> than a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it unclear that I am critical of the portrayal of Lunars in prior Editions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a chimeric Lunar goes far beyond that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimerae are a mess; everything from the idea of &quot;let's create an exclusive category of out-of-theme powers for a bunch of unplayable NPCs&quot; to how they're just so <i>boring</i>; no personality, no aspirations, just a random ball of flesh and teeth rolling around like a carnivorous Katamari Damacy, with no reference to the actual narrative of the Lunar Exalted whatsoever. They don't even serve well as any sort of existential threat, since the assumed default of the Lunar play experience was as somebody who has had the risk neutralised entirely.<br /> <br /> I mean jeez, what was even the point of an Essence 6 Chimera Knack? How was it ever going to be possible for them to become so powerful?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:03:57-07:00","id":104859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104622#post104622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars embody classic, simple themes, and beasts are part of it. Much like Solars making the human be fucking awesome, Lunars should make being a beast be fucking awesome, and not some second-rate prize. They are the tigers that hunted and devoured the Primordials, and being a big vortex of ten thousand limbs wearing the Lunar's face just means you're more exotic food.<br /> <br /> Lunars are also the Moon, Moonlight, Lunacy, Madness, and Chaos (and tied to the Wyld, which in my view should be signaled with Charms that tie to it as Sidereals do Heaven, and Abyssals to the Underworld), so I do expect it could be the form of a tiger whose stripes exhude moonlight, whose eyes pour out with essence and whose jaws are adamant... but it'd still be a goddamn tiger. (EDIT: Or the fluid, shimmering, wolf-but-unreal-wolf, fluid, size-changing fighting style of The Captain, yes!)<br /> <br /> That should be protected and be awesome. And yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>+5, I like the way you think.<br /> <br /> And for the record, if I describe a DBT form as having a crystalline or electric form, that doesn't mean I'm no longer talking about a crystal wolf or an electric jaguar or something vaguely animalish anymore. I think the idea that you would adopt these features only if you think &quot;animals are boring&quot; comes from a misunderstanding about Lunar shapeshifting. For one thing, there are Knacks to change the look and abilities of your DBT form. For another, regardless of your resemblance to your spirit shape, Lunar soak-boosting Knacks like HBR and Charms like Armor-Forming Technique rely on physical transformation to achieve what they do. Something you don't necessarily know if you haven't ever played one before, because just looking at illustrations, you never see Seven Devils Clever turn into a fox of molten fire or whatever.<br /> <br /> Also, Lunars can forge Graces for themselves and learn Fair Folk Charms beginning at E5. If there was anything stopping them from being<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104622#post104622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a tiger whose stripes exhude moonlight, whose eyes pour out with essence and whose jaws are adamant.. or the fluid, shimmering, wolf-but-unreal-wolf, fluid, size-changing fighting style of The Captain</div> </div> </div> </div>...it no longer exists after that point. With Fair Folk shaping, you can make your DBT be <i>a wolf of smoke lit from within by crackles of lightning,</i> if you seriously wanted to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104853#post104853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it unclear that I am critical of the portrayal of Lunars in prior Editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've really just been talking about Lunars as they exist presently, and look like they may exist in 3.0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104853#post104853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chimerae are a mess; everything from the idea of &quot;let's create an exclusive category of out-of-theme powers for a bunch of unplayable NPCs&quot; to how they're just so <i>boring</i>; no personality, no aspirations, just a random ball of flesh and teeth rolling around like a carnivorous Katamari Damacy, with no reference to the actual narrative of the Lunar Exalted whatsoever. They don't even serve well as any sort of existential threat, since the assumed default of the Lunar play experience was as somebody who has had the risk neutralised entirely.<br /> <br /> I mean jeez, what was even the point of an Essence 6 Chimera Knack? How was it ever going to be possible for them to become so powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Chimeric Lunars go way beyond that&quot; was like an afterthought to the main comment, which was about Lunars in general. But please note this quote from John M\u00f8rke:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also realize that one of the reasons people search so furiously for meaning beyond DBT is because a single animal is so constraining, so I am looking at <u>completely redoing Chimeraism so that it is an accepted state, so that players can make cool-looking hybrid monsters with lots of different traits.</u> </div> </div> </div>Yyyyyeah. In some ways, it sounds like what's being planned for Third Edition Lunars is how I've been playing Second Edition Lunars all along. I'm cautiously hopeful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-03-2014, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:07:41-07:00","id":104861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104825#post104825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure a lot of people will think this is a good comment, but in reality it's the complete opposite of the truth. In the entire 2nd Edition setting, there is really nothing more like <i>The Thing</i> than a Lunar. And a chimeric Lunar goes far beyond that.<br /> <br /> *2e*</div> </div> </div> </div>The bit to which you're responding was actually Isator's paraphrasing an official statement from the line's co-developer that EX3 Lunars are not really focused on Alex Mercer nor on The Thing. It's tucked away in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: <b>(HK-87)</b><br /> So is Alex Mercer still a valid character concept for 3E Lunars?</i><br /> <br /> A: <b>(Holden)</b><br /> Not tremendously so. We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a common thing with Lunar discussions I have observed over the past... ever: it's really important not to assume what someone means when they say, &quot;Lunars are/aren't X.&quot; Depending on context (which can clarify, but may not), one could be saying anything from &quot;This is how Lunars are/were in 2e,&quot; to &quot;This is how Lunars are/will be, based on comments from the EX3 Team,&quot; to -- with great and depressing frequency -- &quot;This is what I am personally asserting Lunars are/were/will be.&quot; The third of which a) may or may not have firm grounding in one or both of the prior two, and b) is often delivered with <i>the sincere belief</i> that it has firm grounding in one or both of the prior two.<br /> <br /> I realize this is obvious and a concern at all times -- especially around the corner of an edition change -- but it really comes up with nigh omnipresence* in Lunar discussions. It feels pertinent to stress that. I have collectively seen pages lost to this kind of misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> * Seriously. Really common. Like, anyone who's thinking about a clever meta commentary about these discussions? Something in the vein of, &quot;Even conversations about Lunars often turn into things other than you thought them to be?&quot; It has been noted before. Many times. I'm not saying don't share such things (I'll probably be amused, regardless), just underscoring how well-worn this ground is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:09:00-07:00","id":104863,"title":"","content":"Okay, I have to say that after reading all this, you don't understand what the spirit shape is, at <i>all.</i> It's not something you alter on a whim to create some nightmarish amalgamation of Knacks and Kewl Powerz to feed your desire to not feel left out because your <i>entire splat is fucked because of the above focus</i>, it's an animal that resonates with you on a primal level, chosen at the moment you Exalt.<br /> <br /> It is <i>not</i> something you change lightly, as that leads directly to Chimeradom, and the loss of your ability to play your PC, as your Storyteller reaches across and takes your sheet away, because your PC is now an NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:11:32-07:00","id":104866,"title":"","content":"Wait, there are people who like Lunar as the Wyld Exalted @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:17:20-07:00","id":104869,"title":"","content":"I will happily tell those people to fuck right off. The Lunar Exalted are still <i>human</i> at their core, not a randomly shifting mass of tentacles and penii vaguely shaped in a human form.<br /> <br /> To be honest, one of the biggest concerns I have for Lunars in 3E is the idea that the Chimera will be an <i>accepted</i> part of Lunar society, instead of something to be avoided, like it has been for the last thirteen years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:25:06-07:00","id":104874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104853#post104853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it unclear that I am critical of the portrayal of Lunars in prior Editions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Chimerae are a mess; everything from the idea of &quot;let's create an exclusive category of <b>out-of-theme</b> powers for a bunch of unplayable NPCs&quot; to how they're just so <i>boring</i>; no personality, no aspirations, just a random ball of flesh and teeth rolling around like a carnivorous Katamari Damacy, with no reference to the actual narrative of the Lunar Exalted whatsoever. They don't even serve well as any sort of existential threat, since the assumed default of the Lunar play experience was as somebody who has had the risk neutralised entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>What theme? What the hell is this mysterious <i>Lunar theme</i> you keep talking about? Isator, what IS the Lunar theme? What sort of concepts does it inspire and enable beyond recreating several cherry-picked characters from source material John an Holden happen to like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:25:33-07:00","id":104875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104863#post104863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have to say that after reading all this, you don't understand what the spirit shape is, at <i>all.</i> It's not something you alter on a whim to create some nightmarish amalgamation of Knacks and Kewl Powerz to feed your desire to not feel left out because your <i>entire splat is fucked because of the above focus</i>, it's an animal that resonates with you on a primal level, chosen at the moment you Exalt.<br /> <br /> It is <i>not</i> something you change lightly, as that leads directly to Chimeradom, and the loss of your ability to play your PC, as your Storyteller reaches across and takes your sheet away, because your PC is now an NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant DBT and had already been editing the comment. But anyway... have you read your signature lately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:25:52-07:00","id":104876,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the main reason that some people look to The Thing and Alex Mercer as inspirations for Lunars over Medusa or the Chimera or the Hydra is that the former got to be on the covers of their respective media while the latter were big and generically-menacing and received maybe a paragraph or two of description and characterization before the <i>real </i>stars of the show killed them in a fit of testosterone poisoning, after which they were promptly forgotten except possibly as components of the hero's bling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:30:42-07:00","id":104879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104861#post104861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit to which you're responding was actually Isator's paraphrasing an official statement from the line's co-developer that EX3 Lunars are not really focused on Alex Mercer nor on The Thing. It's tucked away in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, somewhere.<br /> <br /> This is a common thing with Lunar discussions I have observed over the past... ever: it's really important not to assume what someone means when they say, &quot;Lunars are/aren't X.&quot; Depending on context (which can clarify, but may not), one could be saying anything from &quot;This is how Lunars are/were in 2e,&quot; to &quot;This is how Lunars are/will be, based on comments from the EX3 Team,&quot; to -- with great and depressing frequency -- &quot;This is what I am personally asserting Lunars are/were/will be.&quot; The third of which a) may or may not have firm grounding in one or both of the prior two, and b) is often delivered with <i>the sincere belief</i> that it has firm grounding in one or both of the prior two.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I was just calling Isator out for assuming my meaning. I guess I'm guilty as well.<br /> <br /> What exactly does that mean, though? Isator invoked <i>the Thing</i> to paraphrase what I was talking about doing... and what I have in mind actually seems in line with what they've said so far, so I'm kind of confused now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:31:35-07:00","id":104880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104869#post104869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, one of the biggest concerns I have for Lunars in 3E is the idea that the Chimera will be an <i>accepted</i> part of Lunar society, instead of something to be avoided, like it has been for the last thirteen years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of two minds on this:<br /> <br /> The first is starting to be won over by the idea that there's <i>way</i> too much baggage assigned to the idea of a Lunar with a syncretic spirit shape (which is to say, one informed by a coherent blend of animals features). Somewhere along the line, I feel as though too much was put on the idea of Lunars who resemble the actual Chimera. What the drive behind doing so might be, I could not say (possibly something to do with how spirit shapes inform Charm cascades).<br /> <br /> The other side is still attached to the idea that a Lunar might be consumed by their own power, which might be found in the basic concept and accompanying motifs of the chimera, as well as a basis for the moonsilver tattoos.<br /> <br /> Mostly though, I want the latter to be more firmly rooted to the actual Lunar concept and context. I want it to still leave something that has an actual <i>character</i>. I kind of want it to happen mostly on the inside.<br /> <br /> Because I'm still won over by this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And at first it was this heady rush where the might of a thousand beasts and a hundred gods and devils was coursing through you, and it was totally awesome? And then a bunch of guys showed up and did their level best to murder you? And then while you were on the run your power started to feel more and more like a thousand beasts and a hundred gods and devils running riot in your mind and spirit, and you had trouble commanding it? And then the other Lunars found you, and you had to go through that harrowing process of visions and the agony of having mystic silver tattooed into your skin to fix your Exaltation? </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I wonder at the possibility that a Lunar who wants to shift their Totem might need to remove or disable their tattoos, and the stigma might come from the fear of what crept into you while they were gone...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:32:24-07:00","id":104881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104859#post104859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> +5, I like the way you think.<br /> <br /> And I feel I should clarify something: Isator's comment that you were replying to is not really disagreeing with my take as much as it is misunderstanding my take, on the assumption that whenever I describe a DBT form as having a black diamond or electric form, I'm no longer talking about a black diamond wolf or an electric jaguar but something inherently non-animal related. I do think it comes from a misunderstanding about Lunar shapeshifting. For one thing, there are Knacks to change the look and abilities of your DBT form. For another, regardless of your resemblance to your spirit shape, Lunar soak-boosting Knacks like HBR and Charms like Armor-Forming Technique rely on physical transformation to achieve what they do. Something you don't necessarily know if you haven't ever played one before, because just looking at illustrations, you never see Sevin Devils Clever turn into a fox of molten fire or whatever.<br /> <br /> Also, Lunars can forge Graces for themselves and learn Fair Folk Charms beginning at E5. If there was anything stopping them from being</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another thing that needs to die. I can still remember how disgusted I was with it back when it showed up as a thing ten years ago. I have not stopped hating it since. Fortunately, all Wyld connections are off for the next edition, it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, I've really just been talking about Lunars as they exist presently, and look like they may exist in 3.0. </div> </div> </div>And everyone else has been noting their distaste for this. I became so irritated with the presentation as-is that I made a document describing changes one could make to the Alchemical Charms in order to derive something not Silver Solar, and I find that it's neater and closer in focus. I'd still change few things, though, since this thread is giving me a mad hate-on for Knacks that allow you to assume shapes outside animals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Chimeric Lunars go way beyond that&quot; was like an afterthought to the main comment, which was about Lunars in general. But please note this quote from John M\u00f8rke:<br /> <br /> Yyyyyeah. In some ways, it sounds like what's being planned for Third Edition Lunars is how I've been playing Second Edition Lunars all along. I'm cautiously hopeful. </div> </div> </div>Something tells me that the chimerae he was talking about were the first edition kind and not the knockoffs of John Carpenter's The Thing that second edition inflicted on the game. You know, when you could switch spirit shapes and features of the old bled into the new. Only, without the finger-wagging and arbitrary hate that spirits would heap on you. This would allow you to be like the actual Chimera, or Kerberos, etc., rather than a predatory katamari.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:42:54-07:00","id":104889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104881#post104881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something tells me that the chimerae he was talking about were the first edition kind and not the knockoffs of John Carpenter's The Thing that second edition inflicted on the game. You know, when you could switch spirit shapes and features of the old bled into the new. Only, without the finger-wagging and arbitrary hate that spirits would heap on you. This would allow you to be like the actual Chimera, or Kerberos, etc., rather than a predatory katamari.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't actually see how that differs from what I've been talking about. Really, the only transformation I've even mentioned so far that you and Isator found so distasteful and repellant was (1) having crystaline armor and (2) being able to convert your body to elemental essence. Which is something all Lunars can do at Essence 3, with HBR and Luna's Hidden Face (or at E4 with Hearth-and-Flame Shell if your ST disagrees or you can't find an appropriate form to acquire).<br /> <br /> Being able to do those things is not exactly 2e chimerism in the first place, nor is it <i>the Thing</i>, and I don't think they're in any way incompatible with what's been said about the direction for 3E Lunars, so where are your objections even coming from? It sounds like what I have in mind is totally in line with the direction Lunars are taking in the next edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-03-2014, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:47:52-07:00","id":104895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104875#post104875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant DBT and had already been editing the comment. But anyway... have you read your signature lately?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Your comeback to my statement is to tell me to read my signature?<br /> <br /> Dude, that refers to a thread ten years old, asking about a specific canon question that devolved into a long, fun discussion.<br /> <br /> It does not apply here. That said, I'm done here. I will not be replying to you on this again. You do not know what the Hell you're talking about from a canon perspective, and have been dropping your own interpretations of it in from the get-go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:56:58-07:00","id":104902,"title":"","content":"Also, Saur Ops, I wasn't going to respond to this before, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104509#post104509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't put spirit shapes off. They're totemic to a character. You have them from the moment of Exaltation, like your anima banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but I didn't say <i>acquire it as a spirit shape</i>. I said <i>acqure the shape</i>. Presumably the same way you acquire every other shape in your Heart's Blood library. I don't even understand why you'd interpret that to be my meaning here. Especially right after I'd just said I wouldn't allow it as a spirit shape?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104509#post104509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you need to read the text of the mutation again. It mentioned crystal lattices as an option, just like how flight can net you wings or a helium bladder for LTA static lift, or any number of other possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, and &quot;crystal&quot; means &quot;diamond&quot; in what vocabulary? I mean I thought about adding &quot;(by the way yes, I know it says it can be crystal)&quot; in the original comment you're replying to, but I figured it would just be useless cluttering. I guess it was actually necessary to point out, to avoid future argument, that I do know what it says and that having a crystalline lattice structure doesn't actually mean having the hardness of diamond, in my judgment as ST, especially when the same mutation covers <i>ice.</i><br /> <br /> I mean do we really need to be arguing about things like this? Honestly it just seems like you're going out of your way to find fault here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-03-2014, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T10:58:34-07:00","id":104945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104895#post104895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Your comeback to my statement is to tell me to read my signature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104895#post104895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, that refers to a thread ten years old, asking about a specific canon question that devolved into a long, fun discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104895#post104895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not apply here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104895#post104895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm done here. <u>I will not be replying to you on this again</u>. You do not know what the Hell you're talking about from a canon perspective, and have been dropping your own interpretations of it in from the get-go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering your opinion is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104863#post104863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your entire splat is fucked</div> </div> </div> </div>and you haven't had one positive thing to say on the entire thread, I kind of feel like that's not altogether a bad thing. Sorry we could not see eye to eye though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:43:34-07:00","id":104978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104902#post104902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:<br /> Yeah but I didn't say <i>acquire it as a spirit shape</i>. I said <i>acqure the shape</i>. Presumably the same way you acquire every other shape in your Heart's Blood library. I don't even understand why you'd interpret that to be my meaning here. Especially right after I'd just said I wouldn't allow it as a spirit shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes it even worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OK, and &quot;crystal&quot; means &quot;diamond&quot; in what vocabulary? I mean I thought about adding &quot;(by the way yes, I know it says it can be crystal)&quot; in the original comment you're replying to, but I figured it would just be useless cluttering. I guess it was actually necessary to point out, to avoid future argument, that I do know what it says and that having a crystalline lattice structure doesn't actually mean having the hardness of diamond, in my judgment as ST, especially when the same mutation covers <i>ice.</i><br /> <br /> I mean do we really need to be arguing about things like this? Honestly it just seems like you're going out of your way to find fault here. </div> </div> </div>Mineral hardness does not reliably, absolutely correlate to higher soak. Any relatively strong crystal is going to give some measure of protection, but there are other aspects of material behavior to consider in protection, like ductility and the general ability of the material to flex and not instantly break if its structure flexes a tiny, little bit. What's more, you also have to keep in mind that adamant, aka magic, indestructible diamond, exists, and is likely going to make normal diamond seem weak in comparison, with the added benefit of it not chipping or cracking nearly so easily. Against any of the magical materials, diamond is peanuts.<br /> <br /> I mean, you could go on arguing about how it would probably give a bit more soak, but I could then argue that the Lunar could roar at it such that the vibration causes the diamond to crack, shatter, and or explode like a crystalline statue left out for World Whale Keening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-03-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:06:38-07:00","id":104993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104978#post104978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just makes it even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before you say that, ask yourself whether it's possible that you're just misinterpreting it again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104978#post104978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mineral hardness does not reliably, absolutely correlate to higher soak. Any relatively strong crystal is going to give some measure of protection, but there are other aspects of material behavior to consider in protection, like ductility and the general ability of the material to flex and not instantly break if its structure flexes a tiny, little bit. What's more, you also have to keep in mind that adamant, aka magic, indestructible diamond, exists, and is likely going to make normal diamond seem weak in comparison, with the added benefit of it not chipping or cracking nearly so easily. Against any of the magical materials, diamond is peanuts.<br /> <br /> I mean, you could go on arguing about how it would probably give a bit more soak, but I could then argue that the Lunar could roar at it such that the vibration causes the diamond to crack, shatter, and or explode like a crystalline statue left out for World Whale Keening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing with you; I'm pointing out that your criticism (&quot;You can't take a spirit shape later&quot;) is kind of meaningless since I wasn't even slightly suggesting that in the first place.<br /> <br /> And of course it is magical diamond, <i>it grew out of your body and is alive.</i> Presumably, it's a mutation you acquired after eating the heart of a diamond elephant in a southern bordermarch somewhere. How could it conceivably be normal diamond? Think, man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-03-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:23:57-07:00","id":105005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104880#post104880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I wonder at the possibility that a Lunar who wants to shift their Totem might need to remove or disable their tattoos, and the stigma might come from the fear of what crept into you while they were gone...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Chimerism is accepted, but seeking it is stigmatised&quot; seems mighty counterintuitive.<br /> <br /> Better to tie the whole thing into the rage and storming power of the Lunar Exaltation. I'm picturing a thing where the Casteless are always playing with fire, awash with unbound and self-destructive power, while those with Castes have bound their rage to their wills, turning it only against their enemies<sup>1</sup>. The self-destructive bit may involve turning into Koizilla under pressure, but it doesn't <i>have</i> to.<br /> <br /> <sub>1: Mostly.</sub><sub> The Great Curse is still a thing, after all.</sub>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:20:33-07:00","id":105042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105005#post105005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Chimerism is accepted, but seeking it is stigmatised&quot; seems mighty counterintuitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, maybe it's like steroid abuse in career sports, where some degree is tacitly accepted or even encouraged but there are still lines you don't cross because goddamn, son?*<br /> <br /> <sub>*Note to devs: please don't do this, or at least don't make the analogy too blatant; I don't think the Lunars could survive being made into an After-School Special on top of all of their existing issues.</sub><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105005#post105005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><sub>1: Mostly.</sub><sub> The Great Curse is still a thing, after all.</sub></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right, this thread had, like, a <i>topic</i>, didn't it? Well, rhetorical grousing notwithstanding, I'd like for gradual abandonment of identity to be one <i>possible </i>expression of the Lunar Curse - not the only one by any means, but there's a lot of powerful storytelling potential in the risk of 'going native', especially in a setting like Creation where most factions have at least <i>some </i>sympathetic qualities, and there's already a surfeit of splats vying for the limited thematic space of a hero who's SO ANGRY, ALL THE TIME, YOU DON'T EVEN KNOW HOW HARD I CAN BROOD WHEN I <b>REALLY </b>TRY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:30:38-07:00","id":105049,"title":"","content":"Yes. The topic. There was a topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105005#post105005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Chimerism is accepted, but seeking it is stigmatised&quot; seems mighty counterintuitive.<br /> <br /> Better to tie the whole thing into the rage and storming power of the Lunar Exaltation. I'm picturing a thing where the Casteless are always playing with fire, awash with unbound and self-destructive power, while those with Castes have bound their rage to their wills, turning it only against their enemies<sup>1</sup>. The self-destructive bit may involve turning into Koizilla under pressure, but it doesn't <i>have</i> to.<br /> <br /> <sub>1: Mostly.</sub><sub> The Great Curse is still a thing, after all.</sub></div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of chimeraism being an accepted state was quite different. I took it to mean chimeraism might simply be an accepted state for all Lunars, one every Lunar Exalt has to control, rather than being a problem only for the casteless.<br /> <br /> Given how it looks like Lunars are expected to have some kind of rage mechanic, and how Morke says they'll be much more capable in a fight, it's hard to not see those three things being connected.<br /> <br /> I really hope it doesn't turn out that way, though. I like werewolves, but this is Exalted, set in a mythic age of heroes. Lunar Exalted are supposed to be so much more, frankly so much <i>better</i> than werewolves and it just seems so terribly simplistic. If they're going to have a mechanic like that, I'd rather see them changing in more directions and in greater ways than simply getting angry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105042#post105042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, maybe it's like steroid abuse in career sports, where some degree is tacitly accepted or even encouraged but there are still lines you don't cross because goddamn, son?*<br /> <br /> <sub>*Note to devs: please don't do this, or at least don't make the analogy too blatant; I don't think the Lunars could survive being made into an After-School Special on top of all of their existing issues.</sub><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, right, this thread had, like, a <i>topic</i>, didn't it? Well, rhetorical grousing notwithstanding, I'd like for gradual abandonment of identity to be one <i>possible </i>expression of the Lunar Curse - not the only one by any means, but there's a lot of powerful storytelling potential in the risk of 'going native', especially in a setting like Creation where most factions have at least <i>some </i>sympathetic qualities, and there's already a surfeit of splats vying for the limited thematic space of a hero who's SO ANGRY, ALL THE TIME, YOU DON'T EVEN KNOW HOW HARD I CAN BROOD WHEN I <b>REALLY </b>TRY</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from loss of identity, what other possible explanations would you suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:47:17-07:00","id":105066,"title":"","content":"Depending on which source material you're tacking towards, Coyote, Loki, and Anansi are all fine examples of mythic characters whose admirable traits and douchebaggery are two sides of the same coin. Clever but short-sighted, imaginative but lazy, they all tend to act as their own foils to an extent, and while their allies never count them out, they never really count them <i>in</i>, either.<br /> <br /> Also they kinda piss people off sometimes! :V<br /> <br /> My main concern here would be pulling this off as an in-game construct without enshrining &quot;Chaotic Stupid Fishmalk Asshat&quot; as a valid character concept; if you've ever been in a group with someone who likes Kender, you probably understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:38:33-07:00","id":105137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104993#post104993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before you say that, ask yourself whether it's possible that you're just misinterpreting it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That should have been my reaction in the first place, but the eyes sometimes get bleary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course it is magical diamond, <i>it grew out of your body and is alive.</i> Presumably, it's a mutation you acquired after eating the heart of a diamond elephant in a southern bordermarch somewhere. How could it conceivably be normal diamond? Think, man. </div> </div> </div>What's magical about it is that it was alive, not that it had any qualities that made it differ from diamond in any other way. Still doesn't change the fact that gemstones are brittle and tend to chip and break.upon impact with heavy, solid objects, say hammers for the sake of the argument, or a moonsilver thagomizer. If the quality of extreme hardness were modeled by the rules, it would give a substantial soak bonus against cutting, but not against impacts. Which means that any magical materials weapons, and any Lunar with a sufficiently large beast shape that had Claws of the Silver Moon or some other reinforcing Charm active, would smash the diamond monster to bits.<br /> <br /> So be happy with your 6L/6B. It's probably more than you would get otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T20:57:32-07:00","id":105351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104978#post104978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are other aspects of material behavior to consider in protection, like ductility and the general ability of the material to flex and not instantly break if its structure flexes a tiny, little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104978#post104978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">vibration causes the diamond to crack, shatter, and or explode</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105137#post105137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still doesn't change the fact that gemstones are brittle and tend to chip and break.upon impact</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105137#post105137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the quality of extreme hardness were modeled by the rules, it would give a substantial soak bonus against cutting, but not against impacts.<br /> Which means that any magical materials weapons, and any Lunar with a sufficiently large beast shape that had Claws of the Silver Moon or some other reinforcing Charm active, would smash the diamond monster to bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually, none of this is accurate according to the rules, because the basic rules for applying DBT mutations since 2007 have been that you <u>ignore all negative aspects</u> of whatever mutations you're applying, or have we forgetten?<br /> <br /> You know what though? You win. Your tyrant lizard smashes through all obstacles and stomps on any Lunar foolish enough to oppose it. I'm actually sorry to have ever raised the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-04-2014, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T21:10:37-07:00","id":105354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105351#post105351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually, none of this is accurate according to the rules, because the basic rules for applying mutations to your DBT since 2007 have been that you <u>ignore all negative effects</u> of whatever mutations you're applying, or have you forgotten that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You were going out of your way to build up some formless thing made of diamond as a cooler trump card.Even if it were more powerful than Stone Body, gave more soak, or whatever else you had intended on stacking on, it would swiftly become the fuel for another broken build chokepoint revolving around use of Stone Rhino's Skin, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-04-2014, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T21:13:40-07:00","id":105356,"title":"","content":"Yeah okay. You're not even going to acknowledge having completely forgotten about the rules for DBT mutations for the past several comments, are you? That is awesome. You are awesome, Saur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-04-2014, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T21:29:57-07:00","id":105362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105356#post105356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, okay. You're not even going to acknowledge having completely forgotten about the rules for DBT mutations for the past several comments, are you? That is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only bearing on the discussion of lapidary minituae had to do with what kind of soak rating diamond should give and if Stone Body was appropriate to model it for a being made of a hard substance. It'll do. Going further would make getting massive Hardness ratings too easy, unless there were some kind of drawback, which, as you pointed out, DBT eliminates. Thus, DBT would become broken on that front, though as RLF and its ilk show, giving someone just one more choice for building a character doesn't really get things out into the open very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T22:08:30-07:00","id":105377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105362#post105362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lapidary minituae</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually looked that phrase up just now on Google, and there is 1 result. 1 result on the entire internet. You've quite possibly just used it for the 2nd time in all of history. So I guess some respect is due.<br /> <br /> And I must admit I don't actually know what lapidary means, so that also.<br /> <br /> But when I'm playing in your game and you tell me that my body <i>shatters</i> and <i>explodes</i> because I decided to use a DBT mutation, that's when I begin to think that you really might want to re-familiarize yourself with the DBT rules because, you know, that doesn't actually happen, canonically at least, ever.<br /> <br /> But like I said, you win. Your dinosaur wins. Okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T23:04:50-07:00","id":105396,"title":"","content":"Lapidary minutiae: the small or trivial details of precious stones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T23:49:05-07:00","id":105414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105377#post105377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually looked that phrase up just now on Google, and there is 1 result. 1 result on the entire internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is perhaps the first time I have ever had cause to squint at somebody for <i>using</i> Google's &quot;search for exact phrase&quot; function rather than failing to.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/lapidarydef.png\" target=\"_blank\">Use a dictionary.</a> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/minutiaedef.png\" target=\"_blank\">For the individual words</a></i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Google even has &quot;define [x]&quot; as a search option.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T00:11:11-07:00","id":105418,"title":"","content":"I think there was a thread about Lunars in here somewhere.<br /> <br /> At any rate, my core problem with Lunars, and I think one of the core problems with Lunars in general, is this: shapeshifting is nice, and gives you all sorts of neat tricks, but all of those tricks are inherently physical rather than mental. There's almost no examples of shapeshifting to become smarter. Tony Chopper and Mangaverse Reed Richards are the only two I can think of. This means Lunars are kind of fucked when it comes to a large chunk of areas of character competence, most notably crafting and lore. Shapeshifting has no means of addressing these areas. No other Exalt type is hamstrung in this manner, because all of the others have themes that are able to cover these conceptual spaces without any stretching required. Their themes can be directly applied to all areas of competence, while Lunars are saddled with a theme that only covers being the Dumb Brute Exalted and the Sneaky Rat Exalted, forcing them to make up the missing areas of competence by being Silver Solars.<br /> <br /> This is why it is highly important that Lunars have a theme that can be described beyond shapeshifting and that can be applied across all of their Charms the way that the other Exalts are able to apply the theme of &quot;superhuman excellence/demonic power/manipulating destiny/power over death and the dead/control of the elements&quot; across all of their Charms. The only problem is <i>I have no idea what that theme could possibly be</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","user":"Couch","date":". 04-04-2014, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:35:29-07:00","id":105490,"title":"","content":"Oh, wait, I meant to say before:<br /> <br /> The only reason I thought of the idea that having a chimera spirit shape could be somewhat risky is just because I'd still like it if it neither seemed like every Lunar should have it, or make it seem like they're unnecessarily constraining themselves if they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:36:48-07:00","id":105493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105377#post105377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually looked that phrase up just now on Google, and there is 1 result. 1 result on the entire internet. You've quite possibly just used it for the 2nd time in all of history. So I guess some respect is due.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: That is known as a Googlewhack. Although since the term has been used here it won't be long before it isn't anymore. Still fun though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:41:46-07:00","id":105497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105377#post105377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when I'm playing in your game and you tell me that my body <i>shatters</i> and <i>explodes</i> because I decided to use a DBT mutation, that's when I begin to think that you really might want to re-familiarize yourself with the DBT rules because, you know, that doesn't actually happen, canonically at least, ever.<br /> <br /> But like I said, you win. Your dinosaur wins. Okay?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... this is just a shot in the dark, but, I assume you didn't read the post you're responding to past the part that confused you. Right? Because what you're saying doesn't follow. Like at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:27:41-07:00","id":105545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105414#post105414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is perhaps the first time I have ever had cause to squint at somebody for <i>using</i> Google's &quot;search for exact phrase&quot; function rather than failing to.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/lapidarydef.png\" target=\"_blank\">Use a dictionary.</a> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/minutiaedef.png\" target=\"_blank\">For the individual words</a></i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Google even has &quot;define [x]&quot; as a search option.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I made it pretty clear that I had not looked it up because I didn't care to, not because I don't know what a dictionary is or for that matter how to search for a word meaning on Google. I was making an observation that he apparently had a better vocabulary than I did. Is that okay to do, without getting jumped on by some random forumite and criticized for my apparent inability to use a dictionary, an inability that you've almost certainly assumed doesn't actually exist? Seriously, why would you even post a comment like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:33:49-07:00","id":105547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105497#post105497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... this is just a shot in the dark, but, I assume you didn't read the post you're responding to past the part that confused you. Right? Because what you're saying doesn't follow. Like at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, another new friend. Are you following the conversation, by any chance? Are you aware of what I was responding to? In particular the fact that Saur Ops had just spent the last several pages arguing that applying a hypothetical <i>diamond body</i> mutation to your DBT form would come with serious drawbacks such as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=104978#post104978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could go on arguing about how it would probably give a bit more soak, but I could then argue that the [tyrant lizard] could roar at it such that the vibration causes the diamond to crack, shatter, and or explode like a crystalline statue left out for World Whale Keening.</div> </div> </div> </div>...blissfully unaware of the actual rules regarding DBT mutations, which explicitly forbid any such negative effects? And when I pointed out that, no, you actually <u>can't</u> argue that unless you're forgetting how DBT works, he bravely abandoned the line of argument and reframed his position while avoiding any admission of error?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105493#post105493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: That is known as a Googlewhack. Although since the term has been used here it won't be long before it isn't anymore. Still fun though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone gets it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-04-2014, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:35:44-07:00","id":105682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105545#post105545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I made it pretty clear that I had not looked it up because I didn't care to, not because I don't know what a dictionary is or for that matter how to search for a word meaning on Google. I was making an observation that he apparently had a better vocabulary than I did. Is that okay to do, without getting jumped on by some random forumite and criticized for my apparent inability to use a dictionary, an inability that you've almost certainly assumed doesn't actually exist? Seriously, why would you even post a comment like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was unaware that pointing to the existence of a dictionary in the face of someone who, from context (bearing in mind that this is the Internet and thus <i>I can assume nothing about a poster's presence of mind</i>) seemed to have forgotten that such things exist in easy reach with the advent of online reference technology in the course of making a sarcastic-ass &quot;okay, you win, now what?&quot; post that only served to inform the forums that they had a gap in their vocabulary and reassert their already-known position (in a fashion that seemed intended to construe their counterpart as some kind of jargonoid) constituted anything so refined as criticism.<br /> <br /> You made it utterly unclear, for the record, considering that your choice of words to convey this information was &quot;I don't know what that word means&quot; and not &quot;I didn't bother to look up what that word means.&quot; Your attempt to shame me out of joining an ongoing discussion because you don't know me is noted, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105547#post105547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular the fact that Saur Ops had just spent the last several pages arguing that applying a hypothetical <i>diamond body</i> mutation to your DBT form would come with serious drawbacks such as:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>I mean, you could go on arguing about how it would probably give a bit more soak, but I could then argue that the [tyrant lizard] could roar at it such that the vibration causes the diamond to crack, shatter, and or explode like a crystalline statue left out for World Whale Keening.</i></span></b><br /> <br /> ...blissfully unaware of the actual rules regarding DBT mutations, which explicitly forbid any such negative effects? And when I pointed out that, no, you actually <u>can't</u> argue that unless you're forgetting how DBT works, he bravely abandoned the line of argument and reframed his position while avoiding any admission of error?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm going to go ahead and continue to cast aspersions on your reading comprehension, considering that the line you're quoting concerns a hypothetical extramechanical rebuttal to a hypothetical extramechanical argument, i.e. saying that adding more soak than the mutation actually adds because of a thing that the mechanics do not involve would be a pointless claim because by the nature of it not being supported by the mechanics an equally unsupported argument could be applied concerning a viable stunt to counter that introduction of elements beyond the scope of the mutation.<br /> <br /> That you chose to then respond to this with an<i> actual</i>\u200b extramechanical argument unsupported by the text (which disregards the difference between &quot;negative effects of a mutation&quot; - e.g. being slowed down by heavy natural armor-plating - and &quot;things people could use a stunt for&quot; - breaking someone's crystal armor to some degree by way of an incredibly loud and resonant roar) is an irony you seem to have gleefully kickflipped past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:49:01-07:00","id":105701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105682#post105682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm going to go ahead and continue to cast aspersions on your reading comprehension</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105682#post105682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">considering that the line you're quoting concerns a hypothetical extramechanical rebuttal to a hypothetical extramechanical argument, i.e. <u>saying that adding more soak than the mutation actually adds</u></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I wasn't talking about adding more soak than the mutation <i>actually</i> adds because there is no actual <i>diamond body</i> mutation in the first place. Presuming you read the earlier comments, you might have noticed that I'd been describing a hypothetical, not one that actually exists, but one presumably to be added as per the supported mechanics of adding mutations according to the rules. If you're not aware, the ability of players to come up with their own mutations is not extramechanical. It is, in fact, fully mechanical and supported, and actually encouraged according to the core rulebook.<br /> <br /> And,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105682#post105682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was unaware that pointing to the existence of a dictionary in the face of someone who, from context (bearing in mind that this is the Internet and thus <i>I can assume nothing about a poster's presence of mind</i>) seemed to have forgotten that such things exist in easy reach</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really trying to say that it was your genuine, earnest, well-meaning assumption that I'd forgotten I had access to a dictionary or could search for individual words rather than whole phrases, and you were just trying to be helpful? No, it wasn't. Get real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105682#post105682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you chose to then respond to this with an<i> actual</i>\u200b extramechanical argument unsupported by the text (which disregards the difference between &quot;negative effects of a mutation&quot; - e.g. being slowed down by heavy natural armor-plating - and &quot;things people could use a stunt for&quot; - breaking someone's crystal armor to some degree by way of an incredibly loud and resonant roar) is an irony you seem to have gleefully kickflipped past.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was actually no discussion of stunt mechanics until you brought it up just now. But you know that, don't you? I mean, presuming you read the earlier comments before replying, you know that. And you did read them, right? So yeah.<br /> <br /> The argument was that having crystaline armor as a DBT mutation would make a character especially vulnerable to sound, among other things. Which, of course, is kind of inaccurate because DBT mutations don't work that way, at all. If Saur Ops had been talking about stunting, he would have said that when I pointed it out. Instead, he instantly abandoned that whole line of argument without comment, because he suddenly realized it was based on his having forgotten the mechanics of DBT mutations.<br /> <br /> Even if he had been talking about stunting, the idea that you can just roar as a stunt and cause someone's DBT form to shatter and explode is kind of hard to find support for in any published rules I know of, unless there have been some recent provisions for, like, 50-dice stunts, and I don't know of any, do you?<br /> <br /> I realize I'm getting kind of irate about this but seriously, how many of these stupid arguments do I need to put up with? I mean do you have any friends you'd like to invite to the thread so they can make similar criticisms? I'd like to know how many more I need to get through before I stop being constantly told I don't know what I'm talking about by people who legitimately don't know what they're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-04-2014, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:51:24-07:00","id":105760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105490#post105490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason I thought of the idea that having a chimera spirit shape could be somewhat risky is just because I'd still like it if it neither seemed like every Lunar should have it, or make it seem like they're unnecessarily constraining themselves if they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Levi, haven't you always been a firm proponent of the idea that characters, from their internal presence, should have drives and desires and limits beyond what is mechanically apparent or optimal? Isn't this the same as beating somebody over the head with insistence that somebody's Essence should be higher than it is?<br /> <br /> Couldn't NPC Lunars just not want to or manage to shift their spirit shape? Aren't players likely to just desire the aesthetic purity of a singular animal for its own sake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:08:23-07:00","id":105775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105760#post105760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't NPC Lunars just not want to or manage to shift their spirit shape? Aren't players likely to just desire the aesthetic purity of a singular animal for its own sake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't chimerism simply not be a path to power?<br /> <br /> I seriously don't see why it'd be a path to power to begin with, except maybe in the sense that you can give your tiger totem a poisonous serpent for a tail, which is slightly better than <i>not</i> having a poisonous tail.<br /> What I expect chimerism to <i>be</i> is a means of redefining the self, of changing the trajectory of one's own power. No need for it to be DBT volume two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 04-04-2014, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:11:15-07:00","id":105777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105414#post105414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is perhaps the first time I have ever had cause to squint at somebody for <i>using</i> Google's &quot;search for exact phrase&quot; function rather than failing to.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/lapidarydef.png\" target=\"_blank\">Use a dictionary.</a> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/minutiaedef.png\" target=\"_blank\">For the individual words</a></i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Google even has &quot;define [x]&quot; as a search option.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that looking for an exact phrase can be useful. For one thing, how people use a phrase in context can often tell you more about it than a dictionary entry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:11:25-07:00","id":105778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=105775#post105775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously don't see why it'd be a path to power to begin with, except maybe in the sense that you can give your tiger totem a poisonous serpent for a tail, which is slightly better than <i>not</i> having a poisonous tail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, sounds like it might come back to bite you in the ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T06:10:16-07:00","id":115811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103367#post103367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those topics where I feel like it will be vastly easier to speculate once the corebook is out. There are two big lacunae in the way of guesses: we don't know what Lunars look like in Third Edition, and we don't know what the Solar Curse looks like in Third Edition. The dev comments on these two subjects have been interesting, but they're pretty thin grounds for extrapolation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, discussion will certainly be made easier after the corebook is out. But it's not impossible, either.<br /> <br /> We know that Solars are meant to evoke the greatest of Greek heroes, including their fits of excessive passion and other overreactions. We don't know the precise mechanical form this will take, but we know the character behind the mechanics and the inspiration behind that character.<br /> <br /> I just want to see if we can guess at the character and inspiration behind the Lunar Curse.<br /> <br /> Solars have to struggle against going overboard in anything they do, especially when their power is more than enough to take them exactly that far. Abyssals have to struggle against their fate to kill the world by inches (and miles). Alchemicals have to struggle against losing touch with humanity; Liminals might need to struggle in order to get in touch with humanity in the first place. Sidereals struggle to remain open-minded despite being in a position to &quot;know it all, and know it better than you&quot;.<br /> <br /> But against what does a shapeshifter tend to struggle, when you eliminate &quot;his own shapeshifting&quot; or &quot;the light of the full moon&quot; or &quot;losing his humanity in the face of the beast within&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103122#post103122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Jekyll and Hyde isn't on the table, perhaps Ratkin Rapture is. They were &quot;Gnosis frenzies&quot; that imparted distorted visions and premonitions when the rat was too much in tune with the spirit world. It included a number of effects that would be similar to being delusional, paranoid, etc., in addition to more mystical consequences like tuning out the world of matter and seeing only the spiritual landscape of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying Lunars more closely to the immaterial side of Creation <i>does </i>make sense, since the developers are drawing more inspiration from the Garou and the sources that inspired the Garou.<br /> <br /> Hmm. You've seen the <i>Karas </i>movie, right Saur Ops? Karas already has some similarities to Lunar Exalted, and maybe that includes the special relationship with the immaterial side of his city, and all of the spirits that live on that side of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103477#post103477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the inner struggle of the Lunar might not be a conflict, but rather a side of them that leaves them with a fairly powerful passion for the taboo or the extreme, something that can carry their reason along with it, and that many will allow it to*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting carried away by passion is what the Lunar Limit Break already did, and that didn't work because it was just copying the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Other than the Dragon-Blooded, I'm not sure that struggling to avoid wild flights of abandon and excess makes sense for non-Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> their manifestation of the Curse is something else... Maybe at one time it was being too heavily devoted to and dependent on the Solars, and then informed their evolution through the Second Age along lines of &quot;let's become the monsters everybody is saying we are&quot;...<br /> <br /> Hmm, the natural state of Lunars being highly individual, to the point of needing certain restraints based on their context within relationships to others, with their Great Curse as a force to make them <i>too much</i> what other people might observe them as being, rather than being themselves... </div> </div> </div>A curse of meeting and exceeding people's expectations of them might be very interesting, indeed. Certainly, it would introduce a powerful element to their other struggle, which is to find a new place and purpose in the world.<br /> <br /> It's hard to find yourself if you're constantly struggling to avoid becoming what other people think you should be.<br /> <br /> (It would also be another enormous, ironic allusion to how the player base has been treating the Lunar Exalted since their first splatbook was released.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-19-2014, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T06:33:18-07:00","id":115815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103507#post103507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change of identity isn't really something you can enforce and model mechanically though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is. For a given value of &quot;identity&quot;. Or maybe, &quot;some parts of your identity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Motivations, Intimacies and Virtues are important parts of a character's identity. The place of Virtues within the greater rules system is changing, and Motivations are being replaced with greater variety of Intimacies (a three-by-two grid of Ties and Principles, with Defining, Major and Minor levels of intensity), but these things are still defining for a character.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Curse that targets the Lunar's identity might erode a particular Intimacy each time he suppresses a Virtue, or begin building a new Intimacy every time he suppresses his Major Virtue, or perhaps starts to change the emotion context of his lesser Intimacies every time he acts against (or in favor of) his stronger Intimacies.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Lunar curse won't act up just from turning into animals, as TSk thinks, because that would punish Lunars for using the very power people are playing them for in the first place. If anything, it would be more appropriate for the Lunar Curse to act up when they <i>don't </i>shapeshift.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Curse will also not involve becoming more like the animals they turn into, because I quoted John Morke in the very first post, and he said he's not turning the Lunars into a werewolf &quot;man against inner monster&quot; story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T15:20:05-07:00","id":116146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=115811#post115811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tying Lunars more closely to the immaterial side of Creation <i>does </i>make sense, since the developers are drawing more inspiration from the Garou and the sources that inspired the Garou.<br /> <br /> Hmm. You've seen the <i>Karas </i>movie, right Saur Ops? Karas already has some similarities to Lunar Exalted, and maybe that includes the special relationship with the immaterial side of his city, and all of the spirits that live on that side of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Reading a synopsis right now, and it's hard to shake the urge to classify them as Exigents of City Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T18:13:05-07:00","id":116251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=116146#post116146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Reading a synopsis right now, and it's hard to shake the urge to classify them as Exigents of City Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough.<br /> <br /> Yet a Karas does clearly have a Totem animal and shapeshifts into alternate forms, including a war form. The bond between a Karas and Yurine could be seen as similar to a Lunar/Solar bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}